    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000158618019": {
      "title": "Research Fellow, Grade 1",
      "description": "Griffith University Research Fellow, Grade 1 | SmartRecruiters Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox Research Fellow, Grade 1 Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Brisbane South (Nathan) Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: Institute for Biomedicine and Glycomics - IBG Appointment Type: Fixed Term Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. This position will be within Griffith University's Institute for Biomedicine and Glycomics . The Institute brings together Griffith’s formidable strengths in biomedical research. By combining outstanding discovery and translational research, infrastructure, and training expertise our goal is to deliver real and immediate impacts locally and globally, transforming the lives of people around the world, especially those in disadvantaged communities. Job Description The Research Fellow will work as part of a team on an exciting new project focused on vaccine adjuvant discovery and development funded under an NHMRC Centre of Research Excellence. The position is responsible for testing of large libraries of compounds to facilitate the identification of novel immune potentiating molecules and follow up investigation to further define the action of hit and lead molecules. Research will include in vitro cell-based assays and mechanistic studies, in vivo assays, and application of machine learning/AI approaches to adjuvant discovery. The Research Fellow will also contribute to program and laboratory management. Key responsibilities of this position include: Implementation of cytotoxicity, endotoxin and related assays In vivo immunogenicity and reactogenicity studies in mice Contributing to the development machine learning/AI approaches for compound triaging Contributing to immunological and other assays, as required Data analysis and preparation of research reports, presentation and publications as required Acting as Program Manager for the Centre of Research Excellence This is a fixed term (three years), full-time position based at Griffith University Brisbane South (Nathan) . As Griffith is a multi-site University you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s campuses are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range The full-time salary for a Research Fellow, Grade 1 is in the range $91,705 - $107,420 per annum, plus 17% employer superannuation. The total package is in the range $107,295 - $125,682 per annum. Qualifications The successful candidate will hold a PhD in cell or molecular biology/therapeutic discovery/vaccinology or a related area. In addition to the above, you will demonstrate: Experience in laboratory work including cell culture Demonstrated experience in managing large datasets, including preforming assays and data analysis Demonstrated experience in therapeutic discovery and development approaches A high level of oral and written communication, excellent record keeping and good time management skills to ensure research activities are completed to the highest possible standards and within the required timeframe. Ability to work both collaboratively and independently to meet the requirements of the project. Flexibility to adjust working hours, where required, to meet project objectives and deadlines. Additional Information Why join Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts. Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading. How to Apply At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure your application includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role, in particular, addressing the key criteria as listed in the Qualifications section (above) and the position description Current curriculum vitae/resume which should include: Full name, address, telephone number and email address; Details of education, professional training and qualifications; Employment history, including present position and details of relevant professional, consulting or industry experience; Research interests and list of publications; Research grants awarded and any other relevant information, such as offices held in professional bodies, community services etc. Names and contact details of at least three professional referees (no contact will be made without your permission) Applicants must have unrestricted working rights. Visa sponsorship is not available. Successful candidates may be subject to a criminal history check. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Professor Katherine Andrews on (07) 3735 4420 and/or [email protected] For further application and recruitment advice, please contact Theresa Burke, Talent Acquisition Partner on [email protected] Closing date: Friday, 13 November 2026 at 11.59pm AEST. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share."
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000158438699": {
      "title": "Griffith University Clinic Manager (Psychology and Counselling Clinic)",
      "description": "Griffith University Clinic Manager (Psychology and Counselling Clinic)  | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Clinic Manager (Psychology and Counselling Clinic) Part-time Employment Type: Part Time Department ID: Griffith Health Clinics - GHC Appointment Type: Fixed Term Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. Job Description Griffith Health Clinics is seeking a proactive and organised Clinic Manager to oversee the day-to-day operations of its busy, patient-focused Psychology and Counselling Clinic. Working closely with the Psychology Clinic Director, Internship Coordinators, clinical practitioners and academic staff, you will play a key role in ensuring the effective and efficient operation of the clinics. You will lead administrative processes, support financial and business operations, coordinate clinic resources and facilities, and help maintain compliance with relevant professional standards, legislation and University policies. This is an excellent opportunity for someone who enjoys working in a collaborative environment where operational excellence, patient experience, and student learning are equally important. In this role, you will: Oversee daily administrative activities, systems, and processes to ensure the smooth and efficient running of the Psychology and Counselling Clinic. Coordinate and support clinic administration staff, establish effective workflows and contribute to staff development and performance management. Manage day-to-day financial administration, including invoices, third-party payments, reconciliations, and contractor accounts. Analyse operational data, prepare reports, and provide recommendations to support clinic performance, planning, and business development. Manage clinic access, facilities and infrastructure, and coordinate the onboarding and orientation of staff, students, and researchers. Promote adherence to accreditation standards, professional and ethical guidelines, relevant legislation and University policies and procedures. Liaise with internal and external stakeholders and support clinic marketing, communications and promotional activities. Assist the Psychology Clinic Director with operational matters, policy advice, meetings, and the implementation of agreed actions. About you You are a highly organised and solutions-focused professional with demonstrated experience in operational and administrative management. You bring a proactive approach to problem-solving, strong communication skills, and the ability to build effective relationships with a diverse range of stakeholders. You will also demonstrate: A relevant degree, or equivalent combination of relevant work experience and/or education and training, is required. Experience managing administrative operations, systems and processes, ideally within a healthcare, clinical or professional services environment. Strong organisational and time management skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities in a busy environment. Experience coordinating staff, resources and operational workflows. Sound financial administration skills, including managing invoices, payments, and reconciliations. Well-developed analytical and reporting skills, with the ability to identify opportunities for process improvement. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, with a commitment to delivering a professional, patient-focused service. An understanding of the importance of compliance, confidentiality, ethical practice, and quality standards in a clinical setting. What we can offer This is a part-time position (80% FTE, working four days per week) on a fixed-term contract until 30 June 2027, based at Griffith University Gold Coast location. As Griffith is a multi-site University, you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s campuses are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range The full time equivalent base salary will be HEW Level 6 range $94,966 - $101,295 per annum + 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range $111,110 - $118,515 per annum. Additional Information Why Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: 50% fee discount for work related post graduate Griffith degrees Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts How to apply At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the About You section above and the position description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Applicants must have unrestricted working rights. VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Dr Clare Bell, Psychology Clinics Director at clare.bell@griffith.edu.au. For application and recruitment advice, please contact Jinita Dhall, Talent Acquisition Partner at j.dhall@griffith.edu.au . Closing date: We encourage you to submit your application as soon as possible, as applications will be reviewed as they are received. All applications must be submitted online. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at Griffith University Scientific Officer – Anatomy and Pathology MacGregor, Australia Executive Officer (Digital Health and Innovation) Southport, Australia Research Fellow, Grade 1 Nathan, Australia Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Clinic Manager (Psychology and Counselling Clinic) Parklands Drive, Southport, QLD, Australia Part-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000158436559": {
      "title": "Professor in Health Economics and Director, Centre for Applied Health Economics",
      "description": "Griffith University Professor in Health Economics and Director, Centre for Applied Health Economics | SmartRecruiters Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox Professor in Health Economics and Director, Centre for Applied Health Economics Part-time Primary Location (Campus): Brisbane South (Nathan) Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: School of Medicine and Dentistry - MDP Appointment Type: Continuing Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. The School of Medicine and Dentistry strives to prepare the next generation of professionals and practitioners to tackle health and healthcare challenges in an ever-changing world. As a community, we are committed to building better health outcomes for all by delivering high-quality education, impactful research and engagement with and for the communities we serve. As articulated in our Strategic Plan, we commit to the University's values and, importantly, to being a School for Country, place, communities and the people we serve. Through our learning and teaching, we strive to produce graduates who are confident, competent and resilient to be agents for change. At our core is a commitment to innovation and excellence in health research. Through leadership and collaboration, we champion research to optimise health in our local and global communities. Our mission is to engage in ground-breaking research aimed at making meaningful improvements to the health of our communities. We are committed to recruiting and retaining the best possible staff; staff who support our educational mission to deliver an outstanding student learning experience and producing competent, compassionate health professional and practitioners. The School of Medicine and Dentistry shares the Health Group and broader University's commitment to excellence, ethical behaviour, and engagement. The Health Group Charter articulates the core values and behaviours we expect in our workforce: inclusion, integrity, performance, respect, and collaboration.  These values and behaviours are embedded in the School's annual Academic Employee Career Development (AECD) / Professional Staff Career Development (PSCD) process and frame staff performance planning and review conversations. Job Description The Centre for Applied Health Economics (CAHE) within the School of Medicine and Dentistry is seeking a Professor in Health Economics and Director, Centre for Applied Health Economics . The Centre has a strong track record in policy-relevant health economics, evaluation and commissioned research. The successful candidate for the role of Professor in Health Economics and Director, Centre for Applied Health Economics will join a collaborative research environment with opportunities to shape strategic direction, strengthen national and international partnerships, and increase CAHE’s visibility and influence with government, professional, industry, community and university stakeholders. This senior leadership role will provide academic, strategic and operational leadership for CAHE as a leading multidisciplinary centre focused on health economics, health technology assessment, commissioned research, translation and health system improvement. The successful candidate will support the Head of School and the Deputy Head of School (Research) in delivering the School’s strategic research KPIs. They will provide academic leadership, fostering a culture of excellence in research, engagement and professional activities. As Professor and Director, the successful candidate will: Set an ambitious strategic direction for CAHE that advances evidence-driven health economics research, evaluation and policy impact. Lead CAHE’s research strategy, including grant pipelines, commissioned research priorities, impact pathways, performance indicators and annual review processes. Grow and diversify external income through nationally competitive grants, commissioned research, health technology assessment, evaluation and strategic partnerships. Build a high-performing, collegial and multidisciplinary research culture that supports staff capability, interdisciplinary collaboration and higher degree research training. Oversee efficient and scalable centre management, including governance, financial planning, workforce planning, project delivery systems and quality assurance. Maintain a high-quality personal research program with excellent publications, external research income, policy and system impact, and timely HDR completions. The is a continuing, full-time position. It is based at the Brisbane South (Nathan); however, as Griffith is a multi-campus University, the successful candidate will be required to work across other campus or partner locations. Griffith University’s campuses are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range The full-time equivalent base salary for Academic Professor (Level E) is $222,445 per annum, plus 17% superannuation. The total FTE package is $260,261 per annum. Qualifications We are seeking applications from candidates who: Possess a doctoral qualification in health economics or a related discipline. Demonstrate a strong track record in health economics research, including high-quality publications, external research funding, policy or practice impact, and HDR supervision commensurate with appointment at professorial level. Have a demonstrated capacity to lead multidisciplinary teams, build strategic partnerships, manage complex programs of work and translate research into policy, practice and system improvement. Additional Information Why Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: 50% fee discount for work related post graduate Griffith degrees Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts How to apply At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the About You section above and the position description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Names and contact details of at least three professional referees (no contact will be made without your permission). Visa sponsorship may be available to the successful candidate. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Professor Chris Carty, Deputy Head of School (Research) via email at: [email protected] or on (07) 567 87219. For further application and recruitment advice, please contact Jinita Dhall, Talent Acquisition Partner on [email protected] . Closing date: Sunday, 29 November 2026 at 11:59pm AEST. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share."
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000158434409": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer in Digital Health",
      "description": "Griffith University Senior Lecturer in Digital Health  | SmartRecruiters Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox Senior Lecturer in Digital Health Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Gold Coast Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: Pro Vice Chancellor (Health) - PVH Appointment Type: Continuing Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. Job Description The Senior Lecturer (Level C) in Digital Health will provide Health Group-level expertise to strengthen digital health education, curriculum design, and teaching delivery across Griffith’s health programs. Reporting to the Director of Digital Health and Innovation, you will work collaboratively with Schools, Program Directors, Course Convenors and teaching teams to align learning outcomes, assessment and learning resources with recognised digital health capability frameworks.  You will support the integration of health informatics, data science, data-enabled care, virtual care, artificial intelligence literacy, interoperability and clinical safety into curriculum and teaching practice, including simulated, technology-enhanced and interprofessional collaborative learning. The role also contributes to teaching and assessment, applied scholarship and research, and partnerships that strengthen workforce capability and improve health outcomes, service quality, equity and health system performance. As a Senior Lecturer (Level C), you’ll work across the Health Group to strengthen digital health education and help prepare students and health professionals for digitally enabled care. Here’s how you’ll make it matter: Strengthen digital health capability across Health Group curricula, working with Schools and teaching teams to map and align learning outcomes, assessment and learning activities with recognised digital health capability frameworks. Contribute to teaching and assessment, and design authentic simulated, technology-enhanced and interprofessional learning experiences that reflect contemporary digital health practice. Build staff and student capability in the safe, ethical and effective use of digital tools, health data and artificial intelligence in health education and practice. Undertake applied digital health scholarship, research and evaluation to inform education, workforce development and health system transformation, and support a strong pipeline of higher degree research students. Develop partnerships with health services, industry, government, professional bodies and communities to support research translation and the safe, equitable and clinically appropriate implementation of digital health innovations. This is a continuing, full time position primarily based at Griffith University Gold Coast. As Griffith is a multi-site University you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s campuses are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range The full-time equivalent base salary will be Academic Level C range $143,418 - $165,374 per annum + 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range $167,799 - $193,487 per annum. Qualifications What matters most is your drive to create a brighter future that benefits all. Through our core principles of excellence, ethics and engagement, you’ll thrive on seeing the direct and lasting impact you’ll have on every community and every future. You will also have: A PhD and demonstrated expertise, standing and relevant experience in digital health education, research or practice. Experience in curriculum design, teaching and assessment, with the ability to align learning outcomes and learning experiences with recognised digital health capability frameworks and competency expectations. Knowledge of contemporary digital health practice, including health informatics, health data and artificial intelligence, and their safe, ethical, equitable and clinically appropriate application in education and healthcare. Experience in applied scholarship, research or evaluation relevant to digital health, together with the communication and collaboration skills to work across academic teams and build partnerships with health services, industry, government, professional bodies and communities. Additional Information Why Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities How to apply At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the qualifications above and the position description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Names and contact details of at least three professional referees (no contact will be made without your permission) Applicants must have unrestricted working rights. VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. Successful candidates may be subject to a criminal history check. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Prof Gary Grant, Director of Digital Health and Innovation at [email protected] . For application and recruitment advice, please contact Jinita Dhall, Talent Acquisition Partner, at [email protected] and quote reference number REF11697Q. Closing date: Thursday, 19 November 2026 at 11:59pm AEST. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share."
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000158213084": {
      "title": "Griffith University Library Services Officer",
      "description": "Griffith University Library Services Officer | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Library Services Officer Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Brisbane City (South Bank QCA) Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: Library Campus Services - ILN Appointment Type: Continuing Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. Job Description Griffith University Library operates five campus libraries and provides services and expertise to the Griffith University teaching, learning and research community. Library Campus Services Team work closely with clients and establish and maintain strong relationships to deliver useful and timely products and services, and access to resources. As a Library Services Officer, Library Campus Services, you will provide a range of frontline services including general enquiries, research assistance, resource access and computing assistance to clients, delivered through face to face, telephone and digital service points. Key Responsibilities Deliver a positive library experience to all library clients, by providing online and on-campus support covering multiple services and resources. Support clients in accessing and using a range of library resources using the library catalogue, electronic databases, and online products. Support clients in developing their initiative and problem-solving ability through fostering information literacy skills at first tier and facilitating their learning journeys. Assist with research and referencing for assignments, direct to self-help resources and escalate when appropriate. Support the supply of Interlibrary loans to other institutions and assist in providing access to materials via course reading lists, as well as contribute to library projects. Use digital literacy skills to diagnose access issues, referring to other teams as required. Undertake regular personal and professional development to enhance knowledge and skills to enable a high level of service in a continuously changing environment. About you The occupant of this position will have completed or be enrolled in an Australian Library and Information Association accredited course with relevant experience, or relevant library experience. What we can offer This is a full-time, continuing opportunity based at Brisbane City (South Bank). However, applicants must also be available to work at other campus libraries including Brisbane City (CBD), Logan and Brisbane South (Nathan). HEW 4 Salary – Base range - $76,126- $80,321 plus17% superannuation. The full package range is - $89,067 - $93,976. Additional Information Why join Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities. Some mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment. Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts. Griffith's strategic goals are to also increase the proportion of women in senior academic and administrative roles and in Science, Technology, Engineering, Mathematics and Medicine (STEMM). Griffith University’s campuses are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. How to apply At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information, please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A cover letter (maximum of two pages) addressing your suitability for the position referring to the job description above and the Position Description . (If applying through Indeed job board, please include your cover letter in your resume). Your current CV/Resume. Applicants must have Australian working rights. Sponsorship is not available for this position and successful candidates may be subject to a criminal history check. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Hugh Stocks, Library Campus Supervisor via email: h.stocks@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Sunday 8th November 2026 at 11:59pm. All applications must be submitted online By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at Griffith University Service Centre Business Services Officer (Brisbane South (Nathan) or Gold Coast) Nathan, Australia Student Connect Officer Nathan, Australia Scientific Officer – Anatomy and Pathology MacGregor, Australia Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Library Services Officer City, Brisbane City QLD 4000, Australia Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000158199189": {
      "title": "Griffith University Service Centre Business Services Officer (Brisbane South (Nathan) or Gold Coast)",
      "description": "Griffith University Service Centre Business Services Officer (Brisbane South (Nathan) or Gold Coast) | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Service Centre Business Services Officer (Brisbane South (Nathan) or Gold Coast) Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Brisbane South (Nathan) Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: Corporate Services Service Centre - SER Appointment Type: Fixed Term Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. Job Description About the Opportunity As a Business Services Officer, you'll be a trusted first point of contact for staff seeking advice, assistance and support across a broad range of Corporate Services and University-related matters. Working within the University's service management platform, you'll respond to operational and transactional enquiries relating to areas such as finance, payroll, purchasing, travel, human resources and other Corporate Services functions. You'll provide accurate information, interpret policies and procedures, resolve enquiries and guide customers through available services and support pathways. You'll be responsible for resolving low to medium complexity requests and enquiries, while coordinating the referral of more complex matters to specialist teams. Throughout the process, you'll ensure customers remain informed and supported, delivering a positive and professional service experience This role also contributes to the ongoing improvement of service delivery by supporting self-service initiatives, maintaining knowledge resources and identifying opportunities to enhance processes and customer outcomes. This position contributes to staff experience, operational efficiency, and the integrity of corporate service delivery across the University through the provision of reliable case management, proactive communication, and accurate resolution of staff requests. The Service Centre Business Services Officer also plays a key role in building team capability by providing coaching and guidance to colleagues within the Service Centre, supporting capability growth and consistency of service. As part of a flexible and dynamic service environment, the incumbent may be required to work across a variety of corporate and HR service areas, supporting workload balance, service improvement initiatives, and organisational priorities. Key Responsibilities Provide high-quality customer service, ensuring user enquires are handled with empathy and clarity, logged accurately, and resolved or escalated promptly to maintain a positive staff and student experience. Maintain accurate records of user requests, cases, incidents, and resolutions in the service management system, and keep staff informed of progress. Provide clear guidance to staff by explaining policies, processes, and required actions in clear, concise terms to ensure understanding and appropriate application. Identify and resolve common payroll and finance issues (e.g., incorrect pay, leave balances, reimbursements) and resolve at first contact where possible. Use sound judgement to interpret issues and apply policy, procedure, or system knowledge to resolve medium-to-high complexity queries. Manage challenging conversations professionally, using negotiation and empathy to reach workable outcomes. Build collaborative relationships with specialist teams (e.g., HR Advisory, Finance, Payroll) to streamline escalations and share knowledge. Provide guidance and support to Service Centre colleagues to build team capability and ensure consistent service quality. Capture new or updated solutions in the Service Management tool, partnering with subject matter experts to maintain accurate knowledge resources. Contribute to continuous improvement by proactively identifying opportunities to make processes more efficient and effective, suggesting practical changes, and supporting service enhancement projects. Promote and demonstrate cultural behaviour in accordance with the Fraud and Corruption Control Framework and the University Integrity program. This includes acting with integrity in undertaking duties and implementing processes to effectively prevent, detect, and respond to fraud and corruption within the University. Be a leading example of the principles and values embodied in the University’s Code of Conduct, and behave, act and communicate at all times to reflect fairness, ethics and professionalism. About you The occupant of this position will hold relevant tertiary qualifications or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and/or education/training. What we can offer This is a full time, fixed term opportunity for 12 months and can be based at either Brisbane South (Nathan) or Gold Coast campus. As Griffith is a multi-site university, you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary HEW 5 Salary - Base range - $82,415.66 - $92,456.55 + 17% superannuation. Full package range is $96,426.31 - $108,174.16. Additional Information Why join Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme Opportunities for internal mobility Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . How to apply Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role please refer to the qualifications above and the position description. Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details For application and recruitment advice please reach out to Laura Whitworth, Talent Acquisition Partner on l.whitworth-matthews@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Sunday 8th November at 11:59pm. All applications must be submitted online. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at Griffith University Placement Officer Southport, Australia Library Services Officer Brisbane City, Australia Training & Development Officer Nathan, Australia Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Service Centre Business Services Officer (Brisbane South (Nathan) or Gold Coast) 170 Kessels Rd, Nathan QLD 4111, Australia Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000157037000": {
      "title": "Senior Research Fellow Acute Care Nursing",
      "description": "Griffith University Senior Research Fellow Acute Care Nursing | SmartRecruiters Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox Senior Research Fellow Acute Care Nursing Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Brisbane South (Nathan) Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: School of Nursing and Midwifery - Nursing - NUR Appointment Type: Fixed Term Company Description Lead the Future of Acute Care Nursing – Joint Appointment Senior Research Fellow with Griffith University and Princess Alexandra Hospital . Griffith University is a progressive, values-led university dedicated to learning, leadership, and innovation. This is your chance to help us achieve our vision to transform lives and add to human knowledge and understanding in a way that creates a future that benefits all. The Griffith School of Nursing and Midwifery is internationally recognised for excellence in education and research. It is consistently ranked among the world’s leading nursing and midwifery schools (#1 in Australia, #6 in the world; 2026 Shanghai Ranking by Academic Subjects). We are committed to advancing practice, policy and research that improves health outcomes for all. Princess Alexandra Hospital (PAH) is a tertiary health care centre, providing care in all major adult specialties to patients throughout Queensland and Australia, except for obstetrics. We are one of Australia’s leading academic and research health centres, providing Clinical Service Capability Framework (CSCF) Level 6 services, with approximately 1,000 beds. PAH is nationally recognised for expertise in trauma management, and we are a major transplantation centre for livers, kidneys, bone, cartilage, and corneas. We also have responsibility for a number of state-wide services including Queensland Liver Transplant Service, Queensland Tissue Bank, Queensland Spinal Cord Injury Service. The ICU is undergoing a major expansion.  The PAH fulfils a significant teaching and research role, undertaking research and educational programs with affiliated universities and institutes. The expanding research profile is characterised by its full spectrum from basic science to clinical care. Job Description Are you ready to shape the next generation of Acute Care Nurses and lead transformative research at a global scale? Griffith University and Princess Alexandra Hospital are seeking a visionary leader to drive innovation, education, and research in Acute Care Nursing through a prestigious joint appointment. We invite applications from outstanding Acute care nursing leaders for a joint appointment as Senior Research Fellow of Acute Care Nursing. This prestigious role will suit a highly regarded academic and clinician who is passionate about advancing acute care nursing research, education and evidence-based practice through strong clinical- academic collaboration. This is a fixed term, full-time position for three years based in Brisbane at Griffith University Brisbane South (Nathan) and Princess Alexandra Hospital. The successful candidate will be required to work across both locations in person as a requirement of the role. Griffith University's sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range The full-time equivalent base salary will be $143,418 - $165,374 per annum plus 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range $167,799 - $193,487 per annum. Qualifications To be successful in this role, you will have excellent communication and interpersonal skills with a demonstrated and extensive commitment to higher education and nursing. In addition, the successful applicant will demonstrate: Possession of a doctoral qualification or equivalent professional experience in nursing or a relevant field. Registration with the Australian Health Practitioner Regulation Agency (Ahpra) as a registered nurse which is to be active and maintained for the duration of the appointment. A demonstrated track-record in the ability to attract external competitive research funding, to supervise research students and to build and lead multidisciplinary research teams in Acute Care Nursing. Additional Information How to apply At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure your application includes the following: A cover letter addressing your suitability for the position (refer to listed qualifications and position description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details detailing your academic and professional history Names and contact details of at least three professional referees (no contact will be made without your permission) Applicants must have unrestricted working rights. VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. Successful candidates may be subject to a criminal history check. Important Information for Applicants Evidence of vaccination (or the ability to be vaccinated) against the following is required: Measles, Mumps, Rubella, Varicella, Pertussis, and Hepatitis B. Tuberculosis screening may be required to determine vaccination needs. Any serious disciplinary history must be disclosed. For further information about this role, please contact Professor Ann Bonner – Head of School, School of Nursing and Midwifery on [email protected] . For application and recruitment advice, please contact Lane Stachow, Talent Acquisition Partner on [email protected] . Closing date: Thursday, 26 November 2026 at 11.59pm AEST. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share."
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000156200779": {
      "title": "Griffith University PhD Scholarship: Centre of Excellence for the Elimination of Violence Against Women",
      "description": "Griffith University PhD Scholarship: Centre of Excellence for the Elimination of Violence Against Women | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . PhD Scholarship: Centre of Excellence for the Elimination of Violence Against Women Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Brisbane South (Nathan) Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: DVC Research - SDV Appointment Type: Fixed Term Company Description The ARC Centre of Excellence for the Elimination of Violence Against Women (CEVAW) is the world’s first centre to tackle the full range of forms of violence against women in Australia and the Indo-Pacific region. CEVAW aims to transform our understanding of the problem by: examining the structural drivers that cause and compound violence against women (VAW) pioneering new, evidence-based approaches to inform trajectory-altering practice and policy. CEVAW will generate fundamental knowledge on the causes of violence, the contexts in which it occurs, and the most effective and efficient responses. This interdisciplinary research will be data-driven, Indigenous-centred and co-designed with partners. CEVAW brings together more than 40 world-leading experts to develop scalable approaches to eliminate violence against women across the legal, security, economic, health and political systems of Australia and the region. By building strategic and strong partnerships with Australian and international research institutions and partner organisations, CEVAW will translate research into innovative tools and strengthened capacity to drive the elimination of violence against women. Located at Brisbane South (Nathan) campus, Griffith University. As Griffith is a multi-site University you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Job Description The ARC Centre of Excellence for the Elimination of Violence Against Women is seeking a highly motivated PhD candidate to join our team and contribute to a significant research project focusing on conflict-related sexual violence (CRSV) in the Indo-Pacific. This project intends to analyse non-legal pathways to survivor-centred justice for CRSV survivors in post-conflict contexts in the Indo-Pacific. Across the region, transitional justice and reparative programs have been enacted with the intention of meeting survivors’ needs, rights, agency, and participation through different programs, including artistic and creative, faith-based, counselling, healthcare, compensation and economic empowerment, restorative justice and mediation. We welcome research project proposals that propose to explore transitional justice and reparative programs in one post-conflict context.  Proposals can also focus on historical contexts (such as the so-called ‘comfort women’ system established and controlled by the Japanese Imperial Army during World War II), contemporary conflicts (including Nepal, the Solomon Islands, Sri Lanka, Timore-Leste, and Vietnam), and frontier wars that have completed or are undergoing truth and reconciliation processes, such as the Yoorrook Justice Commission (Victoria, Australia). For Indigenous Australians interested in this project, there is an opportunity to apply for the Griffith University Indigenous Australian Postgraduate Research Scholarship (GUIAPRS), which offers financial support through the provision of a stipend to Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander research candidates while they undertake a higher degree research program at Griffith University. The project will suit a candidate with an interest in conflict-related sexual violence, transitional justice, human rights, gender and feminist scholarship.  The project will be designed and informed by the CEVAW's four Indigenous research principles: relationships, material benefit, equity, and Indigenous leadership. All scholarship recipients will be located with the Griffith University Node of the ARC Centre of Excellence for the Elimination of Violence Against Women (CEVAW), under the supervision of Professor Sara Davies, Deputy Director (Indo-Pacific Research) and Dr Phyu Phyu Oo, Research Fellow, CEVAW. There will be an additional opportunity for associate supervision from one of the CEVAW Chief Investigators located in five additional CEVAW nodes (Monash University, Curtin University, Australian National University, Macquarie University and University of Melbourne). The PhD candidates will benefit from unique supervision and mentoring opportunities afforded by CEVAW’s Chief Investigators across different Australian universities as well as networking opportunities across academia and industry through conferences and CEVAW’s partner organisations, nationally and internationally. Qualifications The selection of the applicant for the award of a Higher Degree Research Scholarship at Griffith University is based on academic merit and research background. To be successful in this particular role, you will also need to demonstrate: Evidence of conflict-related sexual violence research, advocacy, or practitioner expertise (essential) Experience with mixed or multiple methods research (essential) Expressions of interest are welcome from Australian or New Zealand citizens or Australian permanent residents. Applicants must have completed a Bachelor’s degree with honours equivalent to first-class honours , or a Master’s degree (AQF Level 9) incorporating a significant research component of a standard comparable to a Bachelor honours degree, or be regarded by Griffith University as having an equivalent level of attainment in accordance with Schedule One of the HDR Scholarship Policy . For further information on the eligibility requirements for the program, refer here . Please note : Prior experience with field research in the Indo-Pacific region including Australia and Aotearoa New Zealand (desirable) Authorship on journal publications and/or reports  (desirable) Additional Information About the scholarship The value of the stipend scholarship is $36,000 per annum (full-time, fixed rate) for three years, with the option for an additional CEVAW top up scholarship of $10,000 per annum. For Indigenous Australians interested in this project, there is an opportunity to apply for the Griffith University Indigenous Australian Postgraduate Research Scholarship (GUIAPRS). A full-time GUIAPRS carries an annual stipend of $55,379 (2026 rate), with the option for a CEVAW stipend of $10,000 per annum. What Griffith offers As a scholarship holder, you will study with a University that ranks among the top 2% worldwide and spans across campuses in South East Queensland. At Griffith University, we’ve worked hard to create a culture that will challenge you to be curious, creative and courageous. We also support the professional and personal development of all our HDR candidates and invest in the skills of our people. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. Griffith's strategic goals are to also increase the proportion of women in senior academic and administrative roles and in Science, Technology, Engineering, Mathematics and Medicine (STEMM). EoI process Please do not select the “APPLY” button. All expressions of interest must be submitted to Professor Sara Davies sara.davies@griffith.edu.au containing: Statement addressing your suitability for the project/scholarship Research proposal outlining your proposed research question, a brief literature review on CRSV and non-legal justice pathways and proposed mixed method research design in one more or more conflict affected contexts (1000 words). A writing sample as lead author or co-author (e.g. published paper, thesis, report) Evidence that you have completed a program with the required grades as detailed in the ‘About you’ section A curriculum vitae (CV) using the Griffith CV template . Names and contact details of two referees Closing date for expressions of interest is: 30 November 2026 5pm AEST The preferred applicant will then be invited to apply for the program and scholarship on-line Further information For project related enquiries please contact: Professor Sara Davies Phone: (07) 3735 9785 Email: sara.davies@griffith.edu.au For administration enquiries please contact: Griffith Graduate Research School Email: hdr-scholarship@griffith.edu.au By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at Griffith University PhD Scholarship: Offshore Hybrid Renewable Energy Systems (OHRES): Market-Driven Site Selection and System Integration (Blue Economy CRC) Southport, Australia PhD Scholarships: Machine Vision Nathan, Australia PhD Scholarship:  Validate novel salivary biomarkers for the early detection of liver fibrosis Nathan, Australia Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. PhD Scholarship: Centre of Excellence for the Elimination of Violence Against Women Kessels Rd, Nathan QLD, Australia Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000154912069": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer (Level C) / Associate Professor (Level D) Nursing",
      "description": "The School of Nursing and Midwifery is one of the largest of schools within the Heath Group and Griffith University. Our School has a strong international reputation (ranked #1 in Australia, #6 in the world, 2026 Shanghai ranking), and we are committed to the global development of nursing and midwifery practice, theory and research in positive and visionary ways. The school is seeking to appoint a Senior Lecturer (Level C) or Associate Professor (Level D) in nursing at Griffith University Gold Coast. As a Senior Lecturer (Level C) Nursing, you will contribute to both teaching and research in the school. You will teach and convene courses in undergraduate and postgraduate programs, supervise Honours and Higher Research Degree students, and undertake high impact research aligned with the research strengths of the school. Where required, this position will also act as program coordinator and/or other leadership roles.  In this role, you will: Lead and innovate in nursing education, designing engaging learning experiences that prepare students for contemporary healthcare practice. Conduct and lead impactful research that advances nursing knowledge, influences practice and contributes to improved health outcomes. Provide academic leadership and mentorship, supporting colleagues, research students, and the ongoing development of the nursing discipline. Build strong industry and community partnerships that enhance student opportunities, strengthen workforce connections, and create real-world impact. Drive excellence across teaching, research, and service, contributing to the School’s strategic priorities and reputation as a leader in nursing education. As an Associate Professor (Level D) Nursing , you will also contribute to excellence in teaching, research and academic leadership within the school, driving innovative education and impactful research that strengthens the nursing profession and improves health outcomes. In this role, you will: Lead and conduct high quality research that aligns with the School’s research strengths, attracts competitive funding, and delivers meaningful impact for healthcare policy, practice and communities. Teach and convene courses across undergraduate and postgraduate nursing programs, creating engaging, student-centred learning experiences that support student success and employability. Supervise and mentor Honours, Higher Degree Research (HDR) and postgraduate students, fostering research excellence and developing the next generation of nursing scholars and leaders. Provide academic leadership through program coordination and other leadership responsibilities, contributing to curriculum innovation, quality enhancement and the strategic direction of the School. Build and strengthen collaborations with academic, industry and healthcare partners to enhance research impact, support workforce development and elevate the School’s reputation nationally and internationally. This is a continuing, full-time position based at Griffith University Gold Coast. As Griffith is a multi-site university you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range Senior Lecturer (Level C) Nursing \nThe full-time equivalent base salary will be Academic Level C range $143,418 - $165,374 per annum + 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range $167,799 - $193,487 per annum. Associate Professor (Level D) Nursing \nThe full-time equivalent base salary will be Academic Level D range $172,686 - $190,248 per annum + 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range $202,043 - $222,590 per annum. \n \nFurther to this salary package the School of Nursing and Midwifery are willing to support the right candidate with a range of additional benefits including: Start-up funds Relocation Support (if required) Visa Sponsorship (if required) \n\n To be successful in this role, you will have: Senior Lecturer Level C Hold a PhD in Nursing or a related discipline, together with unrestricted registration as a Registered Nurse with the Australian Health Practitioner Regulation Agency (Ahpra). Evidence of a research track record and demonstratable commitment to teaching excellence, including course coordination and curriculum development. You will have proven success in attracting competitive research grant funding and a track record of publishing high-quality papers, attracting competitive research grant funding, and publishing. Desirable expertise as either an Ahpra endorsement to prescribe as a registered nurse/nurse practitioner, or Infection Prevention and Control or Mental Health or Aged Care nursing. Associate Professor (Level D) Nursing  In addition to the above, you will have: Demonstrate an established research track record, including publication in high-quality peer reviewed journals, success in securing competitive research funding, and evidence of research impact at a national and/or international level. Possess a strong record of teaching excellence in higher education, with experience in curriculum design, course convening, program coordination, and the delivery of innovative, evidence-based learning experiences. Show a proven ability to supervise and mentor Honours and Higher Degree Research (HDR) candidates to successful completion, while contributing to the development of a vibrant research culture. Bring highly developed leadership, collaboration and stakeholder engagement skills, with the ability to build productive partnerships across academic, healthcare, industry and professional communities. \n\n Why Griffith? \nAs a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities How to Apply At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the qualifications above and the position description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details, education or qualification history, employment history including present position and details of relevant professional, consulting or industry experience, evidence of recent academic teaching evaluations, research interests with list of publications, research grants awarded and other relevant information, such as offices held in professional bodies, community services etc. Names and contact details of at least three professional referees (no contact will be made without your permission) VISA Sponsorship will be available to the successful candidate. For further information about this role, please contact Professor Ann Bonner, Head of School at hos.sonm@griffith.edu.au . For application and recruitment advice, please contact Lane Stachow, Talent Acquisition Partner at l.stachow@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Sunday, 22 November at 11:59pm AEST. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. \n\n At Griffith University we believe in, strive for and celebrate the remarkable. We are known for our high impact research, outstanding student experience, our commitment to social justice, and our welcoming environment. We rank in the top 2% of universities worldwide, and we're proud of our remarkable achievements, of our people, and their passion for making a positive difference. Together we contribute to the development of knowledge and learning in an attractive environment which values excellence, equity, diversity, and innovation.",
      "department": "School of Nursing and Midwifery"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000152829909": {
      "title": "Associate Lecturer (Level A)",
      "description": "Griffith University Associate Lecturer (Level A) - Nursing | SmartRecruiters Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox Associate Lecturer (Level A) - Nursing Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Gold Coast Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: School of Nursing and Midwifery - NRS Appointment Type: Continuing Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. The School of Nursing and Midwifery is internationally recognised for excellence in education and research. It is consistently ranked among the world’s leading nursing and midwifery schools (#1 in Australia, #6 in the world; 2026 ShanghaiRanking by Academic Subjects). We are committed to advancing practice, policy and research that improves health outcomes for all. Job Description As an Associate Lecturer (Level A) in Nursing , you will support the delivery of high quality nursing education while contributing to teaching, scholarship, and student success within a collaborative academic environment. In this role, you will: Deliver engaging learning experiences across undergraduate and graduate nursing programs. Facilitate contemporary teaching and assessment practices that support student achievement. Continuously enhance teaching effectiveness through professional development and reflective practice. Contribute to research, scholarship, and professional activities within the nursing discipline. Engage with industry and community partners to support student learning and employability outcomes. This is a continuing, full time position primarily based at Griffith University Gold Coast. As Griffith is a multi-site university you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range The full time equivalent base salary will be Academic Level A range $82,704 - $111,219 per annum + 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range $96,764 - $130,126 per annum. Qualifications To be successful in this role, you will Hold current registration as a Registered Nurse with Ahpra. Possess a Bachelor of Nursing and a postgraduate qualification in nursing (Graduate Certificate or higher) or bring significant relevant clinical and professional experience. Demonstrate strong contemporary nursing knowledge and a commitment to evidence-based practice. Have excellent communication and relationship-building skills, with the ability to work effectively across academic, clinical, and professional environments. Be committed to ongoing professional development, with completion of, or current enrolment in, a master’s degree viewed favourably. Additional Information Why Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Opportunities for internal mobility Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities How to apply At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the qualifications above and the position description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Names and contact details of at least three professional referees (no contact will be made without your permission) Applicants must have unrestricted working rights. VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Professor Ann Bonner, Head of School - School of Nursing and Midwifery at [email protected] For application and recruitment advice, please contact Lane Stachow, Talent Acquisition Partner at [email protected] Closing date: Monday, 9 November at 11:59pm AEST. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share."
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000152827089": {
      "title": "Lecturer (Level B)",
      "description": "Griffith University Lecturer (Level B) - Nursing | SmartRecruiters Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox Lecturer (Level B) - Nursing Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Gold Coast Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: School of Nursing and Midwifery - NRS Appointment Type: Continuing Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. The School of Nursing and Midwifery is internationally recognised for excellence in education and research. It is consistently ranked among the world’s leading nursing and midwifery schools (#1 in Australia, #6 in the world; 2026 ShanghaiRanking by Academic Subjects). We are committed to advancing practice, policy and research that improves health outcomes for all. Job Description The School is seeking to appoint a Lecturer (Level B) Nursing in a teaching focused role, where you will undertake teaching, course coordination and curriculum development. You are expected to have demonstrated clinical nursing expertise and teaching experience. You will also undertake some learning and teaching research or scholarship. If eligible, supervision of Honours and research higher degree student is possible. This is a continuing, full time position primarily based at Griffith University Gold Coast. As Griffith is a multi-site university you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range The full time equivalent base salary will be Academic Level B range $117,076 - $139,031 per annum + 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range $136,979 - $162,667 per annum. Qualifications To be successful in this role, you will: Hold unrestricted registration as a Registered Nurse with Ahpra. Possess a Master's qualification in Nursing (or equivalent) and/or hold, or be nearing completion of, a PhD in Nursing or a related discipline. Demonstrate a track record in tertiary teaching. Desirable is  expertise in infection prevention and control, mental health nursing, or aged care. Additional Information Why Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Opportunities for internal mobility Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities How to apply At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the qualifications above and the position description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Names and contact details of at least three professional referees (no contact will be made without your permission) Applicants must have unrestricted working rights. VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Professor Ann Bonner, Head of School - School of Nursing and Midwifery at [email protected] For application and recruitment advice, please contact Lane Stachow, Talent Acquisition Partner at [email protected] Closing date: Monday, 9 November at 11:59pm AEST.  All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share."
