    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000120831317": {
      "title": "PhD Scholarships: Machine Vision",
      "description": "This research aims to advance knowledge of machine vision for deep visual understanding of natural objects and environments. The primary focus of this role is to undertake fundamental research in visual understanding and multimodal machine learning. Research activities include developing novel deep learning methods for representation learning, vision-language reasoning, fine-grained and ultra-fine-grained visual categorization, and trustworthy AI systems. The candidate will publish high-quality research papers in leading conferences and journals in computer vision and machine learning. Successful candidates will have the opportunity to receive advanced research training and work within a vibrant research environment that includes a team of research fellows, industry collaborators, and PhD students. The position provides opportunities for collaboration with leading researchers and participation in international research communities in computer vision, machine learning, and artificial intelligence. \n\n The selection of applicants for the award of higher degree research scholarships at Griffith University involves consideration of academic merit and research background. To be successful in this role, you should demonstrate strong analytical and problem-solving skills, solid mathematical foundation, and the ability to work both independently and collaboratively in a research environment. Evidence of a passion for computer vision and image processing is essential. Previous experiences in deep learning, visual recognition, multimodal AI, pattern recognition, or data-driven modelling are preferred. Expressions of interest are welcome from domestic and international applicants. Applicants must have completed a Bachelor’s degree with honours equivalent to  first-class honours , or a Master’s degree (AQF Level 9) incorporating a significant research component of a standard comparable to a Bachelor honours degree, or be regarded by Griffith University as having an equivalent level of attainment in accordance with Schedule One of the  HDR Scholarship Policy . For further information on the eligibility requirements for the program, refer  here . Please note : Applicants with academic qualifications in computer science, engineering, applied mathematics, with a publication record in top tier venues such as CVPR, ICCV, ECCV, NeurIPS, AAAI, IJCAI are preferred. International applicants should ensure that English Language Proficiency requirements for the program are met before formally applying. Applicants to research programs will need to show they meet: A minimum overall band score of 6.5 on the IELTS (Academic) with no band score less than 6.0 OR A score of 79 on the internet-based (iBT) TOEFL with no sub-score less than 19 OR A score of no less than 3+ in each skill of the ISLPR (conducted by ISLPR Language Services only) OR A minimum overall score of 176 (no score less than 169) on C1 Advanced  or  C2 Proficiency OR An overall score of 58 in the Pearson Test of English (Academic) with no score less than 50 (applies to tests taken prior to 7 August 2025) OR An overall score of 55 in the Pearson Test of English (Academic) with no score less than 47 (applies to tests taken on or after 7 August 2025) OR An overall score of 70 in the LanguageCert Academic OR An overall score of 59 in the Michigan English Test (MET) . \n\n About the scholarship \nThe successful candidate will be awarded a Griffith University Postgraduate Research Scholarship (GUPRS) or an equivalent scholarship package funded through the ARC Industry Laureate Fellowship. \n \nThe 2026 Griffith University Postgraduate Research Scholarship has an annual stipend of $35,656 (indexed) for a period of up to three years of full-time study. Please see the GUPRS Conditions of Award for more information. A successful International applicant will also be awarded a Griffith University International Postgraduate Research Scholarship to cover tuition fees for up to three years. Please see the GUIPRS Conditions of Award for more information. \n \n EoI process \nPlease do  not  select the “APPLY” button. All expressions of interest must be submitted to yongsheng.gao@griffith.edu.au, containing: Statement addressing your suitability for the project/scholarship Brief research proposal, maximum 2 pages Evidence that you have completed a program with the required grades as detailed in the ‘About you’ section A curriculum vitae (CV) Names and contact details of two referees Closing date for expressions of interest is: Currently Open  The preferred applicant will then be invited to apply for the program and scholarship on-line \n \n What Griffith offers \nAs a scholarship holder, you will study with a University that ranks among the top 2% worldwide and spans across campuses in South East Queensland. At Griffith University, we’ve worked hard to create a culture that will challenge you to be curious, creative and courageous. We also support the professional and personal development of all our HDR candidates and invest in the skills of our people. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. Griffith's strategic goals are to also increase the proportion of women in senior academic and administrative roles and in Science, Technology, Engineering, Mathematics and Medicine (STEMM). \n \n Further information For project related enquiries please contact: \nProfessor Yongsheng Gao \nEmail:  yongsheng.gao@griffith.edu.au For administration enquiries please contact: \nGriffith Graduate Research School \nEmail:  hdr-scholarship@griffith.edu.au \n\n We are currently looking for 4 highly motivated PhD candidates to join the research of “Next-Generation Visual Understanding” funded by the ARC Industry Laureate Fellowship. The successful candidate will join the research team led by an Australian Industry Laureate Fellow and internationally recognized researchers in smart farming, computer vision, machine learning, and artificial intelligence, within the School of Engineering and Built Environment at Griffith University. The research environment is collaborative and multidisciplinary, combining expertise in deep learning, computer vision, data science, and applied AI, and working closely with industry partners, national research institutions, and international collaborators. \n \nThis opportunity will be primarily based at the Brisbane South (Nathan) campus. As Griffith is a multi-site University you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples.",
      "department": "DVC Research"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000071420565": {
      "title": "PhD Scholarship:  Validate novel salivary biomarkers for the early detection of liver fibrosis",
      "description": "We are currently seeking highly motivated PhD candidates to join our research team at Griffith University. This exciting project aims to develop and validate novel salivary biomarkers for the early detection of liver fibrosis. Highlights of working on this project include: Focus on non-invasive, saliva-based diagnostics for liver fibrosis. Integration of clinical collaboration with hospital partners and cutting-edge research in the laboratory. Opportunity to work at the intersection of translational medicine, proteomics, and biomarker development. \n\n The selection of applicants for the award of higher degree research scholarships at Griffith University involves consideration of your academic merit and research background. To be successful in this role, you should have: A strong academic background in Medical Laboratory Science, Pathology, Molecular Pathology, or a closely related field. Demonstrated research experience working at the interface with hospital laboratories and working with clinicians. Evidence of collaborative skills and the ability to work effectively with clinical and laboratory-based research teams. A clear passion for research and a commitment to advancing the field of liver fibrosis paving the way for precision health. Should hold a valid Australian driver's licence. Expressions of interest are welcome from domestic and international applicants. Applicants must have completed, or expect to complete, a bachelors degree with honours equivalent to  first  class honours or a Masters degree (AQF Level 9) incorporating a significant research component of a standard comparable to a bachelor honours degree or be regarded by Griffith University as having an equivalent level of attainment in accordance with Schedule One of the  HDR Scholarship Procedure .  For further information on the eligibility requirements for the program refer  here . Please note : Applicants must have obtained a Master’s degree or an Honours degree in relative fields. A solid background in Medical Laboratory Science, Pathology, Molecular Pathology with an interest in biomarker discovery is required. Some experience in the field of multivariate statistical analysis would be beneficial but is not required. International applicants should ensure that English Language Proficiency requirements for the program are met before formally applying. Applicants to research programs will need to show they meet: A minimum overall band score of 6.5 on the IELTS (Academic) with no band score less than 6.0 OR A minimum score of 575 on the paper-based TOEFL including a score of no less than 5.0 on the TWE OR A score of 79 on the internet-based (iBT) TOEFL with no sub-score less than 19 \n\n About the scholarship \nThe 2025 Griffith University Postgraduate Research Scholarship has an annual stipend of $34,752 (indexed) for a period of up to three years of full-time study. Please see the  GUPRS Conditions of Award  for more information. A successful International applicant will also be awarded a Griffith University International Postgraduate Research Scholarship to cover tuition fees for up to three years. Please see the  GUIPRS Conditions of Award  for more information. \n What Griffith offers \nAs a scholarship holder, you will study with a University that ranks among the top 2% worldwide and spans across campuses in South East Queensland. At Griffith University, we’ve worked hard to create a culture that will challenge you to be curious, creative and courageous. We also support the professional and personal development of all our HDR candidates and invest in the skills of our people. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. Griffith's strategic goals are to also increase the proportion of women in senior academic and administrative roles and in Science, Technology, Engineering, Mathematics and Medicine (STEMM). EoI process \nPlease do  not  select the “APPLY” button. All expressions of interest must be submitted to  c.punyadeera@griffith.edu.au  containing: Statement addressing your suitability for the project/scholarship Research proposal Evidence that you have completed a program with the required grades as detailed in the about you section, including a  copy of your academic transcript A curriculum vitae (CV) using the  Griffith CV template . Names of  two referees Closing date for expressions of interest is:  Tuesday 29 July 2025 5pm AEST The preferred applicant will then be invited to apply for the program and scholarship on-line For project related enquiries please contact: \nProfessor Chamindie Punyadeera \nEmail: c.punyadeera@griffith.edu.au For administration enquiries please contact: \nGriffith Graduate Research School \nEmail:  hdr-scholarship@griffith.edu.au \n\n The Saliva and Liquid Biopsy Group is dedicated to advancing biomarker discovery for metabolic diseases and cancer, with the goal of improving precision health. Our research focuses on identifying and validating biomarkers that enable more accurate patient stratification based on disease risk, prognosis, and treatment response. The successful PhD applicant will be based at the Institute for Biomedicine and Glycomics (IBG), Griffith University, Brisbane South (Nathan) and will work within a collaborative and interdisciplinary environment. As Griffith is a multi-site University you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples.",
      "department": "DVC Research"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000040674965": {
      "title": "PhD Scholarship:  Synthetic biopolymer-protein conjugates for enhanced mucosal delivery of drugs and antigens",
      "description": "We are currently looking for a PhD candidate to develop innovative biopolymer-protein conjugates for enhanced mucosal delivery of drugs and antigens. This will include electrohydrodynamic atomisation for nasal delivery. The primary focus of this role is to design and develop functional biopolymers that target the mucosa and that are amendable toward electrohydrodynamic atomisation to overcome the current drug and antigen delivery limitations. The project aims to enhance the efficacy of biopolymer micro/nanoparticles through precise control of particle size and charge and fill the gap between the fast advancement in nasal drug and vaccine discovery and conventional ineffective delivery techniques. Success in this role requires knowledge in design of functional polymer particles, generation of cell factories as production strains, bioprocess development and characterisation of nanomaterials before and after the nebulising process. \n  \n\n The selection of applicants for the award of higher degree research scholarships at Griffith University involves consideration of your academic merit and research background. To be successful within this role, you will be able to work in bioengineering, microfluidics, and material science. You will have evidence of a passion for conducting high impact research, with strong desire to undertake research in multidisciplinary research. Expressions of interest are welcome from domestic and international applicants. Applicants must have completed, or expect to complete, a bachelors degree with honours equivalent to  first  class honours or a Masters degree (AQF Level 9) incorporating a significant research component of a standard comparable to a bachelor honours degree or be regarded by Griffith University as having an equivalent level of attainment in accordance with Schedule One of the  HDR Scholarship Procedure .  For further information on the eligibility requirements for the program refer  here . Please note : You should have strong background in Material/Biomaterial science and experiences in design, analysis, fabrication and characterization of new material samples. International applicants should ensure that English Language Proficiency requirements for the program are met before formally applying. Applicants to research programs will need to show they meet: A minimum overall band score of 6.5 on the IELTS (Academic) with no band score less than 6.0 OR A minimum score of 575 on the paper-based TOEFL including a score of no less than 5.0 on the TWE OR A score of 79 on the internet-based (iBT) TOEFL with no sub-score less than 19 \n  \n\n About the scholarship \nThe 2025 Griffith University Postgraduate Research Scholarship has an annual stipend of $34,752 (indexed) for a period of up to three years of full-time study. Please see the  GUPRS Conditions of Award  for more information. A successful International applicant will also be awarded a Griffith University International Postgraduate Research Scholarship to cover tuition fees for up to three years. Please see the  GUIPRS Conditions of Award  for more information. \n \n EoI process \nPlease do not  select the “I'm Interested” button. All expressions of interest must be submitted to  v.dau@griffith.edu.au  containing: Statement addressing your suitability for the project/scholarship Research proposal Evidence that you have completed a program with the required grades as detailed in the about you section, including a  copy of your academic transcript A curriculum vitae (CV) using the  Griffith CV template . Names of two referees Closing date of expressions of interest: Friday 7 March 2025 at 5pm AEST The preferred applicant will then be invited to apply for the program and scholarship online. \n \n What Griffith offers \nAs a scholarship holder, you will study with a University that ranks among the top 2% worldwide and spans across locations in South East Queensland. At Griffith University, we’ve worked hard to create a culture that will challenge you to be curious, creative and courageous. We also support the professional and personal development of all our HDR candidates and invest in the skills of our people. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. Griffith's strategic goals are to also increase the proportion of women in senior academic and administrative roles and in Science, Technology, Engineering, Mathematics and Medicine (STEMM). \n \n Further information For project related enquiries please contact: \nDr Van Dau \nEmail:  v.dau@griffith.edu.au \n \nProfessor Bernd Rehm \nEmail:  b.rehm@griffith.edu.au For administration enquiries please contact: \nGriffith Graduate Research School \nEmail:  hdr-scholarship@griffith.edu.au \n\n Working for one of the most influential universities in Australia and the Asia–Pacific region, you will join a University that spans five physical locations in South East Queensland and all disciplines, while our network of more than 200,000 graduates extends worldwide. We have world-class facilities for micro- and nanotechnology and advanced manufacturing. You will conduct the advanced research at the Centre for Cell Factories and Biopolymers, the centre equipped with modern bioprocessing equipment, including cell disruptors, homogenisers, bioreactors, and chromatography system. It is also located in a PC2 laboratory which is equipped with an array of instruments that enable synthetic biology of bacterial production strain. This opportunity will be primarily based at Brisbane South (Nathan). As Griffith is a multi-site University you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples.",
      "department": "DVC Research"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000159794676": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant",
      "description": "Research is the beating heart of every great university. It fuels discovery, deepens understanding, informs student experience and drives the innovations that shape a better world. At Griffith University, we are proud to be at the forefront of this global mission, making significant contributions to Queensland, Australia and the world through groundbreaking research and development and nurturing the next generation of visionary research leaders. The new ARC Centre of Excellence in Transforming Human Origins Research will exemplify this vision by transforming our understanding of why and how our species, Homo sapiens, is the only surviving human on our planet. The Centre will mobilise Indigenous, Global South and Western expertise to examine under- researched regions in Africa, Asia, and Australia. This novel synthesis aims to address how we became a versatile, global species, resilient to profound environmental changes over the last 300,000 years. Outcomes will include new scientific models and revisions to public education and policies about our history, our biological, and cultural relationships to one another, and how we have reshaped ecosystems worldwide. Benefits include a transformed, ethically engaged study of human origins for the betterment of society. Join a globally significant research initiative that is reshaping our understanding of human origins. As Executive Assistant, you will play a pivotal role in supporting the Director and contributing to the successful delivery of the ARC Centre of Excellence for Transforming Human Origins Research. Working across a diverse portfolio of activities, you will provide high-level project coordination and administrative support, helping drive governance, communications, stakeholder engagement, events, reporting, and the monitoring of key actions and deliverables. This role is ideal for a proactive and highly organised professional who thrives in a dynamic environment, enjoys building relationships with diverse stakeholders, and takes pride in enabling strategic and operational success through exceptional coordination and support. Key responsibilities include but not limited to: Provide high-level executive support to the Director, including diary management, domestic and international travel coordination, accommodation arrangements and associated financial administration. Manage day-to-day administrative operations, including information flow, correspondence, financial and HR processes, and the timely coordination of enquiries and actions. Build and maintain effective relationships with internal and external stakeholders, ensuring clear communication and supporting the achievement of Centre objectives. Deliver secretariat support to committees and working groups, including coordinating agendas, preparing documentation, recording minutes and tracking actions. Coordinate Centre events, workshops, conferences and visitor programs, ensuring professional delivery and a positive stakeholder experience. About you \nThe successful candidate will hold a minimum of an associate diploma qualification plus demonstrated experience in an executive support or advanced administrative role, or an equivalent combination of relevant skills, knowledge and experience. You will also have: Demonstrated experience providing high-level executive support in a complex organisation, including diary management, travel coordination, correspondence management and administrative support to senior leaders. Exceptional organisational and time management skills, with the ability to prioritise competing demands, manage multiple tasks simultaneously and meet deadlines with a high degree of accuracy and attention to detail. Proven ability to coordinate administrative operations, including the use of financial, human resources and business systems, while maintaining confidential and sensitive information appropriately. Highly developed written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to prepare professional documentation, liaise effectively with diverse stakeholders and foster positive working relationships. Demonstrated experience providing secretariat support to committees, boards or working groups, including preparing agendas and papers, recording minutes and monitoring actions. Proven ability to coordinate events, workshops, conferences and stakeholder visits, ensuring high-quality planning, administration and delivery. Strong problem-solving skills and initiative, with the ability to work independently under general direction while contributing effectively as part of a team. High level proficiency in Microsoft 365 applications and the ability to quickly learn new systems and processes. Desirable Experience supporting research, higher education, government or grant-funded programs. An understanding of governance, project coordination and stakeholder engagement within a large, complex organisation. Experience coordinating activities involving domestic and international collaborators, visitors or partners. What we can offer \nThis is a fixed term (7 years), 60% part-time position primarily based at Griffith University Brisbane South (Nathan). As Griffith is a multi-site University you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s campuses are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range \nThe full-time equivalent base salary for a HEW Level 5 is in the range $82,415 - $92,456 per annum, plus 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range $96,426 - $108,174 per annum. \n\n Why Griffith? \nAs a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme How to apply \nAt Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the About you section above and the position description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Applicants must have unrestricted working rights.  Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Successful candidates may be subject to a criminal history check. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Deb Murray, Chief Centre Operations Manager at deb.murray@griffith.edu.au . For further application and recruitment advice, please contact Theresa Burke, Talent Acquisition Partner on t.burke@griffith.edu.au . Closing date:   Thursday, 19 November 2026 at 11.59pm AEST. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. \n\n Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. \nGriffith was created to be a different type of university.  You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000159783249": {
      "title": "Senior Platform Engineer - Windows",
      "description": "About the opportunity  The IaaS Product team (Infrastructure as a Service) delivers secure, highly available infrastructure including Windows, Unix, VMware, Cloud IaaS and PaaS, Server and Storage. In this role, you’ll be providing excellent customer service while working in and guiding a team that builds tools and platforms for delivering Windows Servers services onsite and soon in the cloud.   \n \nThe Senior Platform Engineer - Windows' primary focus is operational and project work for management of Windows Servers, applications and Active Directory.  \n \nTo be successful in this role, you will be a motivated IT professional with relevant qualifications and a background in supporting Windows Servers and Active Directory with a strong desire for continuous learning.   \n \n Key Responsibilities  Enjoy engaging with your peers both within your team and across Digital Foundations on a mix of BAU and project work Ability to troubleshoot and work within a small team of engineers.  Be comfortable working with both technical and non-technical stakeholders.  Want the opportunity to uplift your technical skills.  Enjoy solving problems and learning something new every day within a supportive team environment.  Appreciate flexible work-from-home options, with a 60% onsite / 40% remote work split.  About you  Demonstrated experience supporting a large enterprise Microsoft Windows environment  Demonstrated experience using Active Directory, Group Policy and SCCM.  Demonstrated experience in PowerShell and Infrastructure as Code. Programming and scripting skills applied to automation and solution development (Required).  Experience with cloud-based deployments and support (e.g., Azure, AWS) is well regarded.  Experience working in an Agile delivery environment is well regarded.  Software Development and/or DevOps skills are well regarded.  Availability to participate on the Windows on-call roster, approximately every 4-5 weeks, essential.  The occupant of this position will hold a relevant diploma or degree with at least 6 years' subsequent relevant experience. Applicants must have unrestricted work rights for the duration of the appointment and may be subject to a criminal history check.   What we can offer  \nThis is a full-time, continuing opportunity primarily based at the Griffith University Brisbane South (Nathan). As Griffith is a multi-campus University you may be required to work across other locations.  Salary  HEW 8 - Base range - $117,579 - $132,273 + 17% superannuation. Total salary package range $137,567 - $154,759. \n\n Why join Griffith?  \n  \nAs a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer:  Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities  Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment  Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts  Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading  Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme  Opportunities for internal mobility  Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities  At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our  Equity, Diversity and Inclusion  page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s  Modern Slavery Policy .  How to apply  Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following:  A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role please refer to the qualifications above and the position description. Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details  For application and recruitment advice please reach out to Laura Whitworth, Talent Acquisition Partner on l.whitworth-matthews@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Thursday 19th November at 11:59pm. All applications must be submitted online. \n\n Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why.  \nGriffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them.  Why?  Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence.  Digital Solutions is a value-driven strategic IT partner focused on delivering leading digital experiences for our Students, Colleagues and Community. We work within a contemporary operating model and are modernising our technologies and ways of working to create value and build a digital future for Griffith.",
      "department": "Digital Solutions"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000159552019": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer (Level C) - Nutrition and Dietetics",
      "description": "As South East Queensland prepares to host the Brisbane 2032 Olympic and Paralympic Games, Griffith University is seeking an outstanding Senior Lecturer (Level C) in Nutrition and Dietetics to join our high-performing academic team to contribute to the leadership and delivery of our Nutrition and Dietetics program through excellence in teaching, research, professional engagement, and academic citizenship.  As a Senior Lecturer, you will: Deliver high-quality, evidence-informed and student-centred teaching; Develop innovative learning experiences that prepare graduates for contemporary dietetic practice; Support curriculum development, quality assurance, and accreditation activities; Build and maintain partnerships with industry, health services, and professional stakeholders; Lead and contribute to impactful research and supervise higher degree research students; Foster culturally safe, inclusive, and practice-informed learning environments; Contribute to academic leadership within the discipline and School. About You To be successful in this role, you will have: A qualification in Dietetics and a PhD in Nutrition and Dietetics or a closely related field; Accreditation as an Accredited Practising Dietitian (APD) , or eligibility to practise as a dietitian in Australia; Demonstrated excellence in university teaching and curriculum development; An established record of research publications and growing research impact; Experience supervising honours and/or higher degree research students; Contemporary professional experience in one or more areas of dietetic practice, such as clinical nutrition, public health nutrition, community nutrition, food service management, or related fields; Excellent interpersonal skills and a demonstrated capacity to collaborate effectively across disciplines and professions. This is a continuing, full time position primarily based at Griffith University Gold Coast. As Griffith is a multi-site University you may be required to work across other campus locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range \nThe full-time equivalent base salary will be Academic Level C range $143,418 - $165,374 per annum + 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range $167,799 - $193,487 per annum. \n\n Why Griffith? \nRanked among the world's leading universities, Griffith is recognised for its commitment to social justice, innovation, and transformational education. Ranked in the top 2% of universities worldwide, we are proud of our people, our culture, and our focus on producing work-ready graduates who make a difference. You will join a collegial and supportive environment that values excellence in teaching, research, and community impact, while enjoying the lifestyle opportunities of the Gold Coast. How to apply \nAt Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the qualifications above and the position description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Names and contact details of at least three professional referees (no contact will be made without your permission) Applicants must have unrestricted working rights. VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. Applications are encouraged from academics who are passionate about educating future dietitians, advancing impactful research, and contributing to a vibrant and collaborative academic community. Applications from Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islanders are strongly encouraged. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Professor Rozanne Kruger, School of Allied Health, Sport and Social Work at r.krugr@griffith.edu.au . For application and recruitment advice, please contact Lane Stachow, Talent Acquisition Partner at l.stachow@griffith.edu.au Closing date:  Monday, 30 November at 11:59pm AEST.  All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. \n\n Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. \nGriffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. The School of Allied Health, Sport and Social Work is known for excellence in health education, research and clinical practice. Our fully accredited Nutrition and Dietetics program is recognised for innovative teaching, strong industry engagement, and its commitment to embedding Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander perspectives throughout the curriculum. We are proud of our excellent student outcomes, strong research culture, and collaborative team of academics, clinical educators, and researchers. Applicants with expertise aligned to the School's strategic research priorities, including chronic disease prevention, community and public health nutrition, clinical nutrition, implementation science, food systems, nutrition education, or Indigenous health, are encouraged to apply.",
      "department": "School of Health Sciences and Social Work"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000159544072": {
      "title": "Node Administrator",
      "description": "The Griffith University Node Administrator will support the effective operation of the ARC CoE for Quantum Computer Performance and Integration (the Centre), with a primary focus on the Griffith University (GU) Node, through the provision of high-level administrative and operational support for GU-based investigators, researchers and students. The position will also contribute to coordinated Centre-wide administrative, reporting, and professional-service activities, and will build strong working relationships between the Centre and key internal and external stakeholders. The position is a member of the QPI Operations Team. It is line managed at Griffith University by the Node Lead and reports functionally to the QPI Chief Operations Officer, based at UNSW, on Centre-wide operational matters, including Centre reporting, governance processes, administrative standards and Centre events.  Key responsibilities will include:   For the GU Node:  Serve as the primary administrative contact for the Griffith University Node, building strong relationships with researchers, students, stakeholders, and University partners.   Coordinate the day-to-day operations of the Node, including procurement, travel, onboarding, committee support, and administrative systems.   Manage financial administration, including purchasing, invoicing, reconciliations, budget monitoring, and financial reporting.   Support research activities and events, coordinating workshops, seminars, conferences, student support, and stakeholder engagement initiatives.   Deliver governance, reporting, and compliance support, including performance reporting, committee administration, and adherence to University and funding requirements.  For the Centre overall:  In consultation with the Centre Director, COO and Senior Finance Officer:  Support Centre-wide reporting and review activities, including annual reports and major review submissions.   Contribute to Centre-wide financial monitoring and reporting through the provision of accurate Node financial information.   Support the delivery of the annual QPI Workshop, including domestic travel and on-site event coordination as required.  About you  Demonstrated experience in administration, preferably within tertiary higher degree research administration, and experience providing proactive administrative and operational support in a complex research, higher education or comparable environment, including the ability to coordinate across multiple service areas and follow matters through to completion.  Demonstrated experience in financial administration and monitoring, including tracking expenditure against budgets, reconciling accounts and preparing financial reports, preferably in a grant-funded research environment.  Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with a demonstrated commitment to high‑quality customer service and ability to tailor communications for diverse audiences.  Strong organisational skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines while maintaining a high level of attention to detail.  Well-developed computer literacy skills, including the ability to quickly adapt to new systems and technologies.  Demonstrated ability to interpret and apply policies, and experience providing clear guidance and resolution on complex matters.    The successful candidate will hold relevant tertiary qualifications and subsequent relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of relevant skills, knowledge and experience.  What we can offer This is a three (3) year fixed term part time role (0.4 FTE) position based at the Griffith University Brisbane South(Nathan) campus. As Griffith is a multi-site University you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s campuses are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range \nHEW 6 Salary - Base range - $94,966.18 - $101,295.51 + 17% superannuation. Total FTE package range is $111,110.42 - $118,515.75. \n\n Why join Griffith?  \n  \nAs a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer:  Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities  Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment  Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts  Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading  Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme  Opportunities for internal mobility  Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities  At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our  Equity, Diversity and Inclusion  page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s  Modern Slavery Policy .  How to apply  Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following:  A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role please refer to the qualifications above and the position description. Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details  For application and recruitment advice please reach out to Laura Whitworth, Talent Acqusition Partner on l.whitworth-matthews@griffith.edu.au For information specifically about this role, please contact A/Professor Sergei Slussarenko, Node Lead on s.slussarenko@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Sunday 15th November at 11:59pm. All applications must be submitted online \n\n Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why.  \nGriffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them.  Why?  Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence.  The ARC Centre of Excellence for Quantum Computer Performance and Integration (QPI) is a newly established national research initiative bringing together leading scientists, engineers, students and industry partners to accelerate breakthroughs in quantum computing while building the capability and culture that will shape Australia’s quantum future. QPI spans eight Australian university nodes. The Centre works with government agencies, research organisations and industry partners across the quantum computing sector.",
      "department": "School of Environment and Science"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000159541839": {
      "title": "Scientific Officer – Anatomy and Pathology",
      "description": "An exciting opportunity exists for a Scientific Officer – Anatomy and Pathology to join our Anatomy Facilities team. Reporting to the Anatomy Facility Manager, you will play a critical role in supporting anatomy and pathology teaching, research, and laboratory operations. This position provides specialist technical expertise to academics, researchers, and students while ensuring the highest standards of laboratory practice, compliance, and operational excellence. In this role, you will: Prepare, embalm, maintain and catalogue human anatomical and pathology specimens to support teaching, research and outreach activities. Undertake cadaveric dissections and prepare high-quality anatomical prosections for educational purposes. Provide specialist technical support to academic staff, researchers and students within anatomy and pathology facilities. Coordinate the day-to-day operation of laboratories, including equipment maintenance, resource management and laboratory scheduling. Support the administration and delivery of the Body Donation Program, ensuring activities are conducted in accordance with legislative, ethical and university requirements. Maintain accurate records, databases and documentation relating to specimens, laboratory operations and compliance activities. Deliver laboratory inductions, safety training and technical guidance to staff and students. Ensure compliance with workplace health and safety requirements, risk management processes and relevant legislation. Assist with the procurement, monitoring and maintenance of laboratory equipment, consumables and resources. Support the preparation and delivery of Physiology practical sessions, including set-up, pack-down, and coordination of consumables procurement and inventory management. Liaise professionally with funeral directors, external organisations, donors' families, suppliers and other stakeholders. Contribute to outreach activities, workshops, facility tours and other initiatives that promote anatomy and pathology education. Support continuous improvement initiatives to enhance laboratory operations, service delivery and the overall student and researcher experience. About you You are a highly organised and adaptable technical professional with a passion for supporting excellence in education and research. You are comfortable working in a specialist anatomical environment and possess strong interpersonal skills that enable you to collaborate effectively with a diverse range of stakeholders. To be successful in this role, you will bring: A health-related degree with relevant practical experience, or an equivalent combination of qualifications, training and demonstrated expertise. Experience working with human and other biological materials, including knowledge of cadaveric dissection and embalming techniques. Demonstrated laboratory, technical or scientific support experience within a teaching, research, health, or clinical environment. Strong organisational skills with the ability to coordinate multiple priorities and maintain accurate records. Knowledge of laboratory safety practices, risk management processes, and relevant legislation. Excellent communication skills and a commitment to providing high-quality support and service. Confidence using a range of digital systems, databases, and laboratory technologies. This is a full time, continuing position based at Griffith University Brisbane South (Nathan). As Griffith is a multi-campus University you may be required to work across other campus locations. Griffith University’s campuses are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range \nThe full-time base salary for a HEW Level 5 is in the range $82,415 - $92,456 per annum, plus 17% employer superannuation. The total FTE package is in the range $96,426- $108,174 per annum. \n\n Why join Griffith? \nAs a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Opportunities for internal mobility How to apply \nAt Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our  Equity, Diversity and Inclusion  page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s  Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the job description and the  position description ). Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details. Applicants must have unrestricted working rights. Sponsorship is not available for this position. For further information specifically about this role, please contact James Ashaolu, Anatomy Facility Manager (TPH), at j.ashaolu@griffith.edu.au For application and recruitment advice, Lane Stachow, Talent Acquisition Partner at l.stachow@griffith.edu.au Closing date:  Monday, 23rd November at 11:59pm AEST. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. \n\n Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. \nGriffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. Technical Partners Health (TPH) is an essential provision of technical support crossing the whole of  Griffith Health , spanning across three integral streams: Technologies, Operations and Logistics (TOL) Laboratory and Preclinical Experience Simulation and Practical Experience Our team of 50+ technical specialists supports teaching, research, clinics, and learning within purpose-built facilities across multiple campuses.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000159298859": {
      "title": "Research Fellow - Ultrafast/Strong-Field/Attosecond Science",
      "description": "About the opportunity We are seeking a talented and motivated Research Fellow to join a leading research team undertaking pioneering work in ultrafast, strong-field and attosecond science. This role offers the opportunity to contribute to internationally recognised research at the forefront of understanding electron dynamics and chemical processes on attosecond timescales. Working collaboratively with world-class researchers, you will play a key role in the Australian Research Council Discovery Project, \"Attochemistry – Imaging Valence Electrons in Motion\" Through the design and delivery of innovative experiments, you will help advance fundamental knowledge of electron behaviour during chemical transformations, contributing to high-impact research outcomes and strengthening Griffith University's reputation for research excellence. This is an exciting opportunity to access state-of-the-art facilities, collaborate across disciplines, and contribute to breakthrough discoveries in a rapidly evolving field of science. Key responsibilities Conduct high-quality research that advances the objectives of the research program, contributing to innovative discoveries and impactful outcomes within the Centre and associated projects. Develop a strong research profile through the publication of findings in leading international peer-reviewed journals and by contributing to the development of competitive research funding applications. Collaborate with multidisciplinary research teams, providing expertise and contributing to a broad range of research initiatives aligned with the Centre's priorities. Prepare and deliver high-quality research outputs, including publications, conference presentations, technical reports and stakeholder communications. Contribute to teaching, student learning and curriculum activities as required, supporting Griffith University's commitment to academic excellence. Support the supervision, mentoring and development of Higher Degree Research (HDR) candidates, fostering a positive and productive research environment. Provide guidance and oversight to Research Assistants and technical staff to ensure the successful delivery of research objectives. Maintain compliance with all relevant legislation, ethical requirements, laboratory standards, and University policies and procedures, while promoting a safe, inclusive and professional research culture. About you The occupant of this position will hold a PhD or equivalent qualifications/work experience in Ultrafast/Strong-Field/Attosecond science or a related field. Candidates with prior post-doctoral research experience and hands-on operational knowledge of intense ultrafast lasers and/or photon/particle detectors will be favoured. Sponsorship may be offered for the right candidate. What we can offer \nThis is a full time, fixed term opportunity until 30/09/2029 based at Brisbane South (Nathan) campus. As Griffith is a multi-site university, you may be required to work across other locations. \n \nGriffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Research Fellow Grade 2 – Base range - $117,076.11 - $139,031.71 + 17% superannuation. Full package range - $136,979.05 - $162,667.11. \n\n Why join Griffith?  \n  \nAs a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer:  Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities  Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment  Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts  Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading  Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme  Opportunities for internal mobility  Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities  At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our  Equity, Diversity and Inclusion  page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s  Modern Slavery Policy .  How to apply  Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following:  A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role please refer to the qualifications above and the position description. Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details  For further specifics on this role and its responsibilities please reach out to Professor Igor Litvinyuk on i.litvinyuk@griffith.edu.au For application and recruitment advice please reach out to Laura Whitworth, Talent Acquisition Partner on l.whitworth-matthews@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Tuesday 17th November at 11:59pm All applications must be submitted online. \n\n Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why.  \nGriffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them.  Why?  Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence.",
      "department": "School of Environment and Science"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000160122569": {
      "title": "Griffith University Senior Student Administration Officer",
      "description": "Griffith University Senior Student Administration Officer | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Senior Student Administration Officer Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Gold Coast Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: Student and Academic Services - SMO Appointment Type: Continuing Company Description Join Student Life's Student and Academic Services team - a caring and supportive environment. Continuing, 100% (1.0 FTE) Full-time position primarily based at either Brisbane South (Nathan) or Gold Coast. Job Description As Senior Student Administration Officer play a vital role in delivering high-quality administrative support to students across all stages of their academic journey, helping ensure their success and a seamless experience from enrolment to graduation. Key responsibilities include: Manage complex student administration issues and offer expert advice on matters related to enrolment, program variations, progression, and graduation Assess and processing applications such as credit transfers, cross-institutional studies, degree variations, and course substitutions Verify students' eligibility to graduate and coordinate with academic elements and the Graduations Office Engage in activities that support the student journey from recruitment through to graduation Contribute to the delivery and continuous improvement of Student Administration functions Support third-party student administration functions About you Demonstrated experience in student administration within a tertiary education environment, particularly in areas such as credit, enrolment, progression, and graduation. Thorough understanding of academic policies and procedures, including program structures, credit transfer rules, and degree requirements. Demonstrated ability to assess and process complex applications, such as credit transfers, cross-institutional studies, and program variations. Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to interact effectively with students, faculty, and staff. Ability to work in a dynamic environment with competing deadlines. Demonstrated problem-solving skills and attention to detail Strong time management and organizational skills What we can offer This is a continuing position, 100% (1.0 FTE) Full-Time position primarily based at either Brisbane South (Nathan) or Gold Coast.  As Griffith is a multi-site University you may be required to work across other locations. Salary Range The full time equivalent base salary will be HEW Level 5 range $82,415 - $92,456 per annum + 17% superannuation. The salary including superannuation is in the range $96,426 -$108,174 per annum. Additional Information At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Griffith is a values-led, inclusive workplace committed to diversity, equity, and social impact. Our Nathan campus offers a serene environment, with buildings located in the heart of the beautiful Toohey forest. Our Gold Coast campus (Griffith’s largest) has a vibrant, collaborative work culture combined with outstanding lifestyle benefits and is co-located with the Gold Coast University Hospital and light rail access. It includes modern facilities such as: Griffith Health Centre with advanced medical and research technologies A Business School building with a simulated trading room The national Institute for Glycomics Join our friendly, collaborative, and motivated team, where your work truly makes a difference in the lives of our students How to apply Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the Position Description Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details If applying through Indeed, please incorporate your cover letter in your resume. Applicants must have Australian working rights. Sponsorship is not available for this position. Successful candidates may be subject to a criminal history check. Close date: Sunday 15 November 2026 , at 11:59pm AEST. All applications must be submitted online. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Julie Clifford, Manager, Student Administration via email: j.clifford@griffith.edu.au By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at Griffith University Executive Officer - Griffith Sciences Nathan/Gold Coast, Australia Executive Assistant Nathan, Australia Node Administrator Nathan, Australia Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Senior Student Administration Officer Gold Coast or Nathan, Southport, QLD, Australia Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000159988844": {
      "title": "Griffith University Executive Officer - Griffith Sciences",
      "description": "Griffith University Executive Officer - Griffith Sciences | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Executive Officer - Griffith Sciences Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Gold Coast Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: Sciences Academic - SCA Appointment Type: Continuing Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. As an Executive Support Officer, you’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. Job Description About the opportunity Under broad direction, the Executive Officer provides high-level operational, professional and executive support to senior staff, including members of Science Executive, and coordinates activities associated with the office and portfolio. The Executive Officer undertakes high-level project work, develops strategy and position papers, researches complex matters, prepares advice and information for a range of audiences, and supports policy drafting, revision and evaluation. Key Responsibilities Provide high-level strategic advice, executive and professional support to senior staff and the Sciences Executive, contributing to strategic and operational planning, financial and resource management, and providing subject matter and policy advice across Element activities. Support the effective operation of the Sciences Executive and senior leadership forums, including managing workflows arising from meetings and workshops, preparing agendas and minutes, coordinating administrative actions and maintaining oversight of decisions and outstanding actions. Research and analyse complex strategic and operational matters, preparing high-level correspondence, recommendations, reports, briefings, presentations, guidelines, strategy and policy papers, discussion papers and position papers for senior and executive audiences. Lead and manage high-level projects and initiatives, coordinating expertise across the University, managing events and deadlines, monitoring resources, and ensuring agreed outcomes are delivered. Lead continuous improvement in business processes, systems and governance, including developing and implementing complex systems, procedures and local protocols; reviewing and streamlining policy and procedural content; and identifying business improvement and technology-enabled opportunities. Manage and coordinate professional and support staff, including allocating priorities and workloads to ensure timelines are met and required outcomes are delivered. Develop and maintain effective professional relationships and networks across the University and with external stakeholders, professional and community organisations, and clients. This position may be required to take on other responsibilities, commensurate with the expectations of a role at this level, which contribute to the overall objectives of the work unit.  Other duties as directed. Lead and promote compliance with relevant legislation and University policies and procedures, including equity and health & safety and exhibit good practice in relation to same. Be a leading example of the principles and values embodied in the University’s Code of Conduct, and behave, act and communicate at all times to reflect fairness, ethics and professionalism. About you The occupant will hold relevant tertiary qualifications with at least four years’ relevant work experience, or an equivalent combination of relevant skills, knowledge, experience and / or training. What we can offer This is a full time, continuing appointment and can either be based at Gold Coast or Brisbane South (Nathan) campus. As Griffith is a multi-site university, you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary HEW 8 – Base range - $117,579.27 - $132,273.33 + 17% superannuation. Full package range - $137,567.74 - $154,759.79. Additional Information Why join Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme Opportunities for internal mobility Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . How to apply Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role please refer to the qualifications above and the position description. Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details For application and recruitment advice please reach out to Laura Whitworth, Talent Acquisition Partner on l.whitworth-matthews@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Friday 20th November at 11:59pm. All applications must be submitted online. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at Griffith University Senior Student Administration Officer Southport, Australia Senior Data Insights Analyst Nathan, Australia Executive Assistant Nathan, Australia Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Executive Officer - Griffith Sciences Gold Coast or Nathan Campus, Nathan/Gold Coast, QLD, Australia Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000159985609": {
      "title": "Griffith University Senior Data Insights Analyst",
      "description": "Griffith University Senior Data Insights Analyst | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Senior Data Insights Analyst Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Brisbane South (Nathan) Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: Planning and Analytics - FFM Appointment Type: Fixed Term Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. As a Data Insights Analyst, you’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. Job Description The Senior Data Insights Analyst is a senior specialist role within BI & Analytics, providing a dedicated analytical partnership to Student Experience. The role leads the design and delivery of rigorous evaluations, advanced statistical analyses, and modeling that strengthen understanding of student equity, experience, engagement, success, retention, and completion. Working closely with Student Experience leaders, evaluation specialists, program teams, and other University stakeholders, the role determines fit-for-purpose analytical approaches, evaluates the reach and effectiveness of student initiatives, and translates complex findings into clear, practical recommendations. The role applies BI & Analytics standards, governed institutional data, and reproducible analytical methods to build credible evidence about what is working, for whom, under what conditions, and where services or investment could be refined. Key Responsibilities Lead the end-to-end analytical design and delivery of student equity and experience evaluations , from the development of evaluation questions and outcome measures through to statistical analysis, interpretation, reporting, and recommendations. Apply advanced statistical and analytical methods —using R, Python, SQL, or other appropriate tools—to analyze longitudinal, hierarchical, observational, and linked institutional data. Methods may include regression, survival and time-to-event analysis, multilevel and mixed-effects modeling, predictive modeling, quasi-experimental approaches, segmentation, and other techniques suited to the evaluation question and available data. Provide senior methodological advice on evaluation design, comparison groups, counterfactuals, sampling, statistical power, model selection, assumptions, missing data, clustering, bias, sensitivity analysis, and the appropriate interpretation of causal and non-causal findings. Evaluate the reach, implementation, outcomes, and impact of student initiatives , including whether programs are reaching intended cohorts, how outcomes vary between student groups, and how the timing, intensity, sequencing, or combination of supports may influence student outcomes. Use independent professional judgment to select and adapt analytical approaches for complex or previously undefined problems, clearly documenting limitations, uncertainty, evidence strength, and conditions affecting interpretation. Translate analytical findings into clear, decision-ready advice for Student Experience and senior University stakeholders, identifying implications for program design, targeting, coordination, investment, continuation, scaling, redesign, or further evaluation. Build robust and reproducible analytical workflows , including validated analysis-ready datasets, documented definitions and assumptions, reusable code, model diagnostics, quality-assurance checks, and transparent methods that enable findings to be reviewed, repeated, and updated. Partner with Student Experience teams and subject-matter experts to strengthen program logic, evaluation plans, data-collection practices, outcome definitions, and minimum data standards so that initiatives are designed and delivered in ways that support meaningful evaluation. Work with BI & Analytics colleagues to ensure analyses use governed institutional data and consistent definitions , and contribute specialist advice to the development and quality assurance of equity measures, analytical datasets, models, and evaluation standards. Develop dashboards, visualizations, monitoring products, and recurring reports where these support evaluation, communicate findings, or enable ongoing tracking of student outcomes. Dashboarding and routine reporting are supporting capabilities of the role rather than its primary purpose. Undertake targeted research and evidence synthesis to identify emerging analytical methods, sector practices, policy expectations, and external evidence relevant to student equity and experience, and assess their implications for Griffith. Provide technical leadership, peer review, coaching, and mentoring to analysts and project colleagues in statistical practice, evaluation methods, reproducible analysis, quality assurance, and the communication of complex findings, without formal people-management responsibility. Contribute to continuous improvement of University analytical practice by developing reusable methods, templates, guidance, and evaluation approaches that increase analytical rigor, consistency, efficiency, and institutional capability. Operate in accordance with University requirements for privacy, ethics, security, responsible data use, and analytical integrity , exercising particular care when working with sensitive student and equity data. About you to be successful in this role it is essential that you have the below skillset; 5+ years of professional experience in data analysis, business intelligence, or related analytical roles Advanced proficiency in SQL for querying, manipulating, and managing large datasets Demonstrated expertise with at least one BI visualization tool (Tableau, Power BI, Looker, or equivalent) Strong statistical analysis and data modeling capabilities Proficiency in at least one programming language (Python, R, or similar) for data manipulation and analysis Excellent communication and presentation skills with the ability to translate complex data into clear, actionable insights Strong organisational and project management skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities Experience working with stakeholders across different business functions Knowledge and understanding of Equity based government policies desirable skillset; Experience with cloud-based data platforms (Azure) Knowledge of advanced analytics techniques including machine learning and predictive modelling Familiarity with data governance and data quality frameworks Experience in Higher Education or Government industry Relevant certifications such as Google Analytics Certification, Tableau Desktop Specialist, or Microsoft Certified Data Analyst Experience with version control systems and collaborative development environments What we can offer This is a full time, fixed term opportunity for 3 years based Brisbane South (Nathan) campus. As Griffith is a multi-site university, you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary HEW 8 – Base range - $117,579.27 - $132,273.33 + 17% superannuation. Full package range - $137,567.74 - $154,759.79. Additional Information Why join Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme Opportunities for internal mobility Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . How to apply Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role, please refer to the qualifications above and the position description. Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details For application and recruitment advice please reach out to Laura Whitworth, Talent Acquisition Partner on l.whitworth-matthews@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Open until filled. All applications must be submitted online. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at Griffith University Senior Student Administration Officer Southport, Australia Executive Officer - Griffith Sciences Nathan/Gold Coast, Australia Executive Assistant Nathan, Australia Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Senior Data Insights Analyst 170 Kessels Rd, Nathan QLD 4111, Australia Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000160543139": {
      "title": "Associate Lecturer in Acting",
      "description": "Griffith University Associate Lecturer in Acting | SmartRecruiters Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox Associate Lecturer in Acting Part-time Primary Location (Campus): Brisbane City (South Bank QCM) Employment Type: Part Time Department ID: Queensland Conservatorium - QCM Appointment Type: Continuing Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. Job Description One of the Asia-Pacific’s leading music and performing arts schools, Queensland Conservatorium Griffith University (QCGU) offers a comprehensive suite of professionally-oriented and community-resonant opportunities and qualifications in music and performing arts. Its current fields of focus are music (performance, contemporary creative practices, education & community, production & entrepreneurship), acting and musical theatre, with programs embracing community stakeholders from early childhood to senior citizenship including our comprehensive suite of full-time tertiary programs (Bachelor, Masters, PhD) relevant for 800 students. QCGU is seeking an Associate Lecturer (Level A) in Acting to contribute to high-quality teaching, course coordination and the ongoing development of scholarly and/or professional practice within the Acting discipline. On offer is a continuing, 50% part-time position. Ideal candidates will bring substantial professional and/or pedagogical experience in actor training, with the capacity to teach across a range of acting practices, performance contexts and genres. We are particularly interested in practitioners whose artistic and teaching practice can contribute to a contemporary, collaborative and industry-engaged approach to actor training. This teaching focused position will commence 1 February 2027 with the occupant required to undertake full academic responsibilities and related administration for the coordination of courses, programs and associated student activities – including regular use of University IT systems to do so. On campus, face-to-face teaching is required and work patterns for part-time positions are expected to reflect the teaching requirements of the role. Key responsibilities include but not limited to: Foster an outstanding student experience and encourage active participation and engagement in learning and teaching across the spectrum of the University’s undergraduate, and postgraduate program suite facilitating high quality, student-centred learning activities. Support high-quality learning and teaching outcomes for students evidenced by technology enhanced learning, problem oriented, authentic learning and assessment practices. Support a student-centred service culture and establishment of positive, respectful and supportive relationships between staff and students. Promote and enhance student learning experiences through engagement with industry and broader community to develop work integrated learning opportunities and support employability initiatives. This is a continuing, 50% part-time position primarily based at Griffith University Brisbane City (South Bank) Queensland Conservatorium. As Griffith is a multi-site University you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s campuses are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range The full-time equivalent (FTE) base salary for an Associate Lecturer (Level A) is in the range $82,704 - $111,219 + 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range $96,764 - $130,126 per annum. Qualifications The occupant will hold relevant tertiary education qualifications with at least honours or higher or equivalent professional education and experience. You will also have: Demonstrated ability to deliver high-quality teaching and to engage students effectively Proven ability to develop and implement innovative curriculum and teaching materials Demonstrated experience in providing academic support and mentoring to students Commitment to ongoing professional development and engagement in scholarly activities relevant to teaching Ability to work collaboratively with colleagues and contribute to interdisciplinary projects A well-established artistic identity which embraces a diversity of communities, performative contexts and genres. Commitment to making Acting in Queensland matter, both state-wide and within the region that embraces Australasia, Oceania and East, South and Southeast Asia. Demonstrated leadership with the ability to inspire and motivate people to be as engaged with acting as they are able, both individually and collectively. Additional Information Why Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading How to apply At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. In line with the Conservatorium's commitment to inclusion and equity, candidates with identified expertise that speaks to encouraging and supporting students of different abilities or of diverse cultural backgrounds, particularly First Nations, are encouraged to apply. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the About you section above and the position description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Names and contact details of at least three professional referees (no contact will be made without your permission) Applicants must have unrestricted working rights.  Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Successful candidates may be subject to a criminal history check. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Professor Vanessa Tomlinson, Director, QCGU at [email protected] For application and recruitment advice, please contact Theresa Burke, Talent Acquisition Partner on [email protected] . Closing date: Monday, 23 November 2026 at 11.59pm AEST. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share."
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000160786439": {
      "title": "Griffith University Senior Analyst, Research Data and Reporting",
      "description": "Griffith University Senior Analyst, Research Data and Reporting | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Senior Analyst, Research Data and Reporting Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Brisbane South (Nathan) Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: Office For Research - ORE Appointment Type: Continuing Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university.  You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. Job Description The Office for Research delivers professional research support services with functions spanning grants, research development, research ethics and integrity, research outputs, policy, and performance reporting.  The team works closely with academic colleagues and senior managers to address research priorities across the University and provide high-level strategic and administrative support to Griffith researchers in all disciplines and career stages. The Senior Analyst, Research Data and Reporting plays a key role in supporting research administration data and systems across the University by ensuring that research data is collected and stored securely and accurately across various systems in a form that optimises retrieval and reporting capability for both internal reporting and analysis and external compliance returns. As part of the Research Data Management team in the Research Excellence Performance and Systems unit of the Office for Research, as Senior Analyst you will be responsible for the implementation of routine and complex reports and reporting tools that support Office for Research operations in grants management, research development, ethics management, and underpin the development of research policy and strategy. Also, your experience supporting users and systems will contribute to enhancing the existing systems, interfaces, and user support processes. Your key responsibilities in this position include: Assistance in the implementation of effective systems for collecting, storing, and analysing research administration data, testing and optimising datasets and systems required for internal and external evaluations, submissions, Open Data, and other reporting requirements ensuring the University’s data is accurate and complete. Your understanding of the academic environment and experience working at universities or research organisations will be key for working with s academic elements and research centres and institutes, to ensure they understand the requirements for research data collection, verification, and maintenance e.g., research outputs, income, ethics, and compliance. Your expertise will contribute to the preparation and benchmarking analysis required for internal reporting, as well as government evaluations and submissions. Your communication and interpersonal skills will drive connections and liaison with internal units such as Digital Solutions, Library, Planning & Analytics, and others, as well as with system vendors, government agencies and other stakeholders involved in research performance reporting.  You will work closely with the Research Data and Reporting Manager in providing advice to the University on technical compliance issues arising from changes to government guidelines and policies as well as ensuring that Office for Research systems and reports meet University, national and global standards. Your passion for research data will drive initiatives and projects to enhance and support data interfaces that provide unified view of researcher profiles as well as academic performance within the University, while working with the Research Data management team to implement, support, and improve data management and quality assurance processes. About you It is essential for the successful candidate to have demonstrated experience in data management and development roles, ideally in the Australian universities’ context. Relevant postgraduate qualifications or extensive experience or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and/or education/training is required. An understanding of the University environment and research administration, and familiarity and/or experience in using research administration systems and related systems, in particular PeopleSoft, would be highly desirable. In addition to the above, you will have: Demonstrated knowledge and experience in areas of data management and analytics with strong ability in data manipulation and Structured Query Language (SQL), preparing complex reports in relation to compliance requirements or performance assessments and proven ability to work under pressure and meet tight deadlines. Demonstrated knowledge and experience in designing / supporting data integrations, including functional design, testing and ongoing maintenance of interfaces; experience liaising with technical and end user teams with relation to source and target systems and resolution of data integration issues. High level conceptual, analytical, and problem-solving skills and demonstrated ability to translate complex business requirements into effective technical solutions. Experience with a wide range of database, data warehousing and/or business intelligence software and tools (e.g., Microsoft Power BI, Microsoft SQL Reporting Services, Tableau). Demonstrated high-level organisational skills, attention to detail, and a strong ability to independently plan workflow and manage deadlines. Demonstrated high-level communication skills including the ability to liaise with internal and external stakeholders, and communicate technical information to laypersons, as well as the ability to work both in a team environment and independently. Desirable knowledge and skills: Experience with or high-level knowledge of API programming, Google Big Query data warehouse. High level understanding of Open Access principles and institutional repositories Good understanding of external data platforms and databases e.g., ORCID, Dimensions, Scopus and others. Experience working with research administration systems e.g., for managing research grants, ethics protocols or research outputs. Experience working with or high-level knowledge of PeopleSoft HR and Campus Solutions environments. What we can offer This is a continuing, full-time position and will be primarily based at Griffith University Brisbane South (Nathan).  As Griffith is a multi-site University you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s campuses are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range The base salary will be HEW Level 8 in the range $117,579 - $132,273 per annum, plus 17% superannuation. The total package will be in the range $137,567 - $154,759 per annum. Additional Information Why Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme How to apply At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the About you section above and the position description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Names and contact details of at least three professional referees (no contact will be made without your permission) Applicants must have unrestricted working rights.  Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Successful candidates may be subject to a criminal history check. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Zhanna Shldenova, Research Data and Reporting Manager, on (07) 373 58457 or via email: z.shldenova@griffith.edu.au . For further application and recruitment advice, please contact Theresa Burke, Talent Acquisition Partner on t.burke@griffith.edu.au . Closing date: Wednesday, 25 November 2026 at 11.59pm AEST. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at Griffith University Executive Officer - Griffith Sciences Nathan/Gold Coast, Australia Senior Data Insights Analyst Nathan, Australia Executive Assistant Nathan, Australia Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Senior Analyst, Research Data and Reporting 170 Kessels Rd, Nathan QLD 4111, Australia Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000160784869": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Griffith University Administrative Assistant | SmartRecruiters Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox Administrative Assistant Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Brisbane South (Nathan) Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: Institute for Biomedicine and Glycomics - IBG Appointment Type: Fixed Term Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university.  You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. Job Description Griffith University's Institute for Biomedicine and Glycomics brings together Griffith’s formidable strengths in biomedical research. By combining the outstanding discovery and translational research, infrastructure, and training expertise of the Griffith Institute for Drug Discovery, the Institute for Glycomics and biomedical teams from within the former Menzies Health Institute Queensland we will deliver real and immediate impacts locally and globally, transforming the lives of people around the world, especially those in disadvantaged communities. The Administrative Assistant will be responsible for the efficient and effective daily management of the reception desk, the provision of administrative support to the Institute, and co-ordination of associated office duties ensuring high standard service delivery and outcomes. Key responsibilities include: Manage the Institute reception desk effectively and perform reception duties including; greeting visitors, answering and redirecting all incoming calls, management of key and access card registers and managing entry into the Institute’s car parks. Provide high-level administrative support to the Executive Officer including; arranging meetings, events/activities coordination and execution, records management, processing of correspondence and documents, database management and a range of electronic diaries, support with human resource matters such as recruitment and induction of new staff and students. Diary management for senior Executives including all meetings and other commitments, arranging conference registrations and travel, if required. Provide administrative support to Institute Committees as required. Coordinate and submit reimbursement and payment requests and provide ad-hoc support to other members of the Institute as required. Provide back-up and support to the Administration team and undertake other duties as required as relevant to the role. About you The successful candidate will have completion of a diploma or certificate level qualification with relevant work experience, or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and/or training. You will also have: Demonstrated experience in front desk and reception duties, including greeting visitors, managing incoming calls, maintaining access registers, and overseeing car park entry procedures with professionalism and efficiency. Proven ability to provide high-level administrative support. Strong organisational and time management skills. Experience in committee support, including preparing agendas, taking minutes, and coordinating follow-up actions in a timely and accurate manner. Ability to work collaboratively within a team. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills, with a customer-focused approach and the ability to liaise effectively with internal and external stakeholders. What we can offer This is a fixed term (12 months), full-time position and will be primarily based at Griffith University Brisbane South (Nathan). As Griffith is a multi-site University you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s campuses are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range The full-time base salary for a HEW Level 4 is in the range $76,126 - $80,321 per annum, plus 17% employer superannuation. The total package is in the range $89,067 - $93,976 per annum. Additional Information Why Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including leave loading Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities How to apply At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the About you section above and the position description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Applicants must have unrestricted working rights. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Successful candidates may be subject to a criminal history check. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Nina Kristensen, Senior Executive Officer, Institute for Biomedicine and Glycomics at [email protected] . For further application and recruitment advice, please contact Theresa Burke, Talent Acquisition Partner on [email protected] . Closing date: Monday, 23 November 2026 at 11.59pm AEST. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share."
    },
