    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000161225189": {
      "title": "Griffith University Head of Corporate Services Service Centre",
      "description": "Griffith University Head of Corporate Services Service Centre | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Head of Corporate Services Service Centre Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Brisbane South (Nathan) Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: Corporate Services Service Centre - SER Appointment Type: Fixed Term Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. Job Description About the opportunity Reporting to the Director, Human Resources, the Head of Corporate Services Service Centre will lead the delivery and continuous improvement of integrated services across Griffith Assist, Finance, Digital, Campus Operations, and Service Design. This senior leadership role is responsible for creating a seamless, customer-focused service experience for staff and students, driving service transformation, channel integration, self-service and automation initiatives, and embedding best-practice service management through ServiceNow. Working closely with leaders across Corporate Services, you will enhance operational performance, strengthen governance and risk management, and deliver measurable improvements in service quality, efficiency and customer experience. Key Responsibilities Lead the delivery of the Service Centre strategy, driving transformation and continuous improvement initiatives. Partner with the Director, HR to deliver a seamless, customer-focused service experience across multiple channels. Build and embed service design capability to enhance employee and student experiences. Establish and lead best-practice service management frameworks, leveraging ServiceNow to improve performance, efficiency and service quality. Coach and support service owners to use data and insights to drive service excellence and continual improvement. Strengthen governance, risk management and operational controls across key service areas. Oversee assurance activities, ensuring risks, incidents and improvement actions are effectively managed. Build strong partnerships with leaders and stakeholders to align services with University priorities and deliver measurable outcomes. About you You are a proven service delivery leader with significant experience driving large-scale service centre transformation, operational excellence and customer-focused service improvement within a complex organisation. You bring extensive leadership experience, supported by relevant qualifications or an equivalent combination of education and professional expertise. You will demonstrate: Significant experience leading complex service transformation initiatives, including operating model redesign, service integration, digital enablement and continuous improvement. A strong understanding of employee and student lifecycle experiences, with the ability to design and deliver services that are simple, accessible and customer-centric. Expertise in contemporary service management practices, including service design, governance, performance measurement, self-service, knowledge management and automation. Experience implementing and optimising digital workflow and service management platforms such as ServiceNow. A track record of leading organisational change, influencing stakeholders and driving measurable improvements across multiple service teams and business functions. Exceptional leadership, communication and relationship-building skills, with the ability to foster collaboration and deliver strategic outcomes in a complex environment. What we can offer This is a full time, fixed term appointment for 5 years based at  Brisbane South (Nathan) campus. As Griffith is a multi-site university, you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary This is a senior contract and a competitive salary will be negotiated with the preferred candidate. Additional Information Why join Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme Opportunities for internal mobility Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . How to apply Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role please refer to the qualifications above and the position description. Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details For application and recruitment advice please reach out to Laura Whitworth, Talent Acquisition Partner on l.whitworth-matthews@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Monday 23rd November at 11:59pm. All applications must be submitted online. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at Griffith University Associate Lecturer in Acting South Brisbane, Australia Senior Analyst, Research Data and Reporting Nathan, Australia Senior Lecturer (Level C) - Nutrition and Dietetics Southport, Australia Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Head of Corporate Services Service Centre 170 Kessels Rd, Nathan QLD 4111, Australia Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000161218729": {
      "title": "Lecturer Level B - Human Systems and Exercise Physiology",
      "description": "Griffith University Lecturer Level B - Human Systems and Exercise Physiology | SmartRecruiters Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox Lecturer Level B - Human Systems and Exercise Physiology Part-time Primary Location (Campus): Gold Coast Employment Type: Part Time Department ID: School of SHS - Exercise Science - EXS Appointment Type: Continuing Company Description Griffith University is a progressive, values-led university dedicated to learning, leadership, and innovation. This is your chance to help us achieve our vision to transform lives and add to human knowledge and understanding in a way that creates a future that benefits all. We are known for our high impact research, outstanding student experience, our commitment to social justice and our welcoming environment. We rank in the top 2% of universities worldwide and we're proud of our remarkable achievements, of our people and their passion for making a positive difference. Together we contribute to the development of knowledge and learning in an attractive environment which values excellence, equity, diversity, and innovation. The School of Allied Health, Sport and Social Work is a leader in health education, research, and clinical practice, known for its innovative approach and commitment to developing work-ready graduates. With programs spanning Exercise Science, Human Services, Nutrition and Dietetics, Occupational Therapy, Physiotherapy, Rehabilitation Counselling, Social Work, and Speech Pathology, we bring together a diverse team of academics who are pioneering change in their fields. Exercise & Sport at Griffith has played a major role in delivering transformative education to students across Queensland and beyond. We are known for our innovative curriculum, award-winning teachers, high impact researchers, and state-of-the-art facilities. Strong industry partnerships enable us to provide diverse, high-quality education experiences that create confident, safe, and practice-ready graduates. Job Description We are seeking a Lecturer in Human Systems and Exercise Physiology to join our team in a role that contributes to teaching, research and professional practice education. You will play a key role in delivering high-quality student learning opportunities across a range of Health programs. As a Lecturer in Human Systems and Exercise Physiology , you will: Develop and deliver engaging, evidence-based teaching, primarily in Human Systems and Exercise Physiology, for students enrolled in a range of health programs, including Exercise Science, Clinical Exercise Physiology, Physiotherapy, Nutrition and Dietetics, and Biomedical Sciences. Contribute to and support teaching delivery across a range of courses in Exercise Science and Clinical Exercise Physiology. Collaborate with academic staff within the discipline and across disciplines to address professional standards and accreditation requirements Conduct and contribute to research in discipline-related areas Support the discipline to provide culturally safe education and prepare students for culturally safe practice About You To be successful in this role, you will: Bring a passion for teaching and an innovative approach to student learning. You will have experience teaching and/or supervising students in university settings. You will demonstrate expertise in Clinical Exercise Physiology, and a commitment to evidence-based teaching, interprofessional collaboration and culturally safe education. This role suits an applicant with, or nearing completion of, a PhD and an emerging research track record. Applicants with suitable PhD-entry qualifications (e.g., Masters/MPhil) who are interested in undertaking a PhD will also be considered. This is a continuing, part time (50%, 2.5 days per week) position primarily based at Griffith University Gold Coast. As Griffith is a multi-site University you may be required to work across other campus locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. If you are a passionate and forward-thinking academic looking to make a meaningful contribution to education and research, we would love to hear from you. Salary Range The full time equivalent base salary will be Level B range $117,076 - $139,031 per annum + 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range $136,979 - $162,667 per annum. Additional Information Why Join Us? Work in a collaborative and supportive team environment Opportunities for professional development and research growth Engage with interdisciplinary teams and partnerships Contribute to innovative teaching and research Make a real impact by educating the next generation of Health practitioners. The Location & Lifestyle You Deserve This role is based in stunning South-East Queensland at our Gold Coast and City campuses. Enjoy a work-life balance like no other, with access to world-famous beaches, rainforests, and Brisbane, the host city of the 2032 Olympics, all within easy reach. How to apply At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the qualifications above and the position description) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Applicants must have unrestricted working rights. VISA sponsorship is not available for this position. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Associate Professor Surendran Sabapathy, Exercise Science on [email protected] For application and recruitment advice, please contact Lane Stachow, Talent Acquisition Partner at [email protected] . Closing date: Monday, 7th December at 11:59pm AEST.  All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share."
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000161185669": {
      "title": "Griffith University Technical Officer - Simulation and Practical Experience (SPE)",
      "description": "Griffith University Technical Officer - Simulation and Practical Experience (SPE) | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Technical Officer - Simulation and Practical Experience (SPE) Full-time Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: HTS - Simulation and Practical Experience - SIP Appointment Type: Continuing Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. Job Description Looking to step away from shift work, while still using your healthcare skills? Join Griffith University as a Technical Officer - Simulation (Nursing and Midwifery) to support the delivery of realistic learning experiences for Nursing and Midwifery students. This hands-on role involves preparing, maintain and supporting clinical teaching laboratories and simulations spaces ensuring equipment, facilities and consumables are ready for student learning. Perfect for someone who enjoys the practical side of healthcare, this is a technical support role rather than a teaching or clinical care position. No night shifts, no weekends. Weekday hours, with shifts between 7am and 6pm, and a positive work-life balance. Here’s how you’ll make it matter: Prepare and maintain clinical teaching laboratories and simulation environments for Nursing and Midwifery students. Provide technical support for practical classes and simulation-based learning activities. Manage equipment, consumables, stock control and procurement to ensure resources are safe, available and fit for purpose. Promote safe and compliant work practices, supporting Work Health and Safety requirements across learning spaces. Work collaboratively with academic and professional staff to deliver high-quality student learning experiences and continuous improvement initiatives. About you What matters most is your commitment to making a positive impact. You’ll bring practical, reliable and service-focused approach, with experience in healthcare, clinical learning or technical support environments. You take pride in creating safe, well-prepared learning spaces and enjoy hands-on work. With strong organisational skills, attention to detail and a proactive mindset, you can manage competing priorities while delivering high-quality outcomes. You will also have: Relevant health qualification, or an equivalent combination of education, training and experience. Experience providing clinical, laboratory, simulation or technical support, ideally in healthcare, tertiary education or clinical skills environments. Demonstrated ability to maintain safe, compliant learning environments, with strong knowledge of Work Health and Safety practices. Strong organisational, communication and problem-solving skills, with the ability to manage competing priorities and work collaboratively with diverse stakeholders. Practical experience supporting clinical learning spaces, simulation environments, equipment and resources, with proficiency in Microsoft 365 and a willingness to learn new technologies. Experience supporting Nursing, Midwifery or other Health discipline simulation activities is highly regarded. A current driver’s licence is desirable. What we can offer This is a continuing, full-time position primarily based at the Griffith University Logan. As Griffith is a multi-site university you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary Range The full time equivalent base salary will be HEW Level 4 range $76,126 - $80,321per annum + 17% superannuation. The total FTE package will be in the range $89,067 - $93,976 per annum. Additional Information Why join Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities Griffith's strategic goals are to also increase the proportion of women in senior academic and administrative roles and in Science, Technology, Engineering, Mathematics and Medicine (STEMM). How to apply At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role (please refer to the qualifications above and the position description ) Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details Applicants must have unrestricted working rights. Sponsorship is not available for this position. For further information specifically about this role, please contact Anna Marshall, Team Leader - Clinical Skills and Simulation at anna.marshall@griffith.edu.au. For application and recruitment advice, please contact Lane Stachow, Talent Acquisition Partner at l.stachow@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Sunday, 29 November at 11:59pm AEST. All applications must be submitted online. Please allow at least 1 – 2 weeks from the closing date to expect an application update. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at Griffith University Head of Corporate Services Service Centre Nathan, Australia Lecturer Level B - Human Systems and Exercise Physiology Southport, Australia Program Delivery Officer Meadowbrook, Australia Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Technical Officer - Simulation and Practical Experience (SPE) 68 University Dr, Meadowbrook QLD 4131, Australia Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    },
    "https://jobs.smartrecruiters.com/GriffithUniversity/744000161179179": {
      "title": "Griffith University Program Delivery Officer | SmartRecruiters",
      "description": "Griffith University Program Delivery Officer | SmartRecruiters Sorry, Internet Explorer 11 is no longer supported by SmartRecruiters Please update to one of the following browsers: Google Chrome Microsoft Edge Apple Safari Mozilla Firefox You can find details about supported web browsers here . Program Delivery Officer Full-time Primary Location (Campus): Logan Employment Type: Full Time Department ID: Online Strategy - ONL Appointment Type: Continuing Company Description Every institution values excellence. What matters most is why. Griffith was created to be a different type of university. You’ll find we’re about leading research, academic excellence, and the transformative power of education. But what sets us apart is why those things matter and how you’ll achieve them. Why? Griffith brings together exceptional minds like yours from across the globe and from all walks of life. Here, we do incredible work, questioning and challenging, always in the pursuit of excellence. Job Description About the opportunity Located within the Provost portfolio, the Online Strategy Unit (OSU) drives the creation and implementation of a transformative vision for online education programming through strategic leadership and oversight of the growth and expansion of the University’s online learning programs. Building on Griffith’s already well-recognised synchronous and hybrid online offerings, the Unit is developing a suite of degrees in partnership with all Academic Groups for delivery in a cutting edge, high quality, technology-enabled and student-focused learning design model. Key Responsibilities We are seeking a proactive and student-focused Program Delivery Officer to support the successful delivery of Griffith Go programs. In this role, you will help ensure a high-quality experience for students by coordinating key elements of program delivery, including: Providing student learning administration Implementing student engagement strategies Supporting student outcomes and success Responding to learning-related enquiries Coordinating student learning analytics and leveraging data to provide effective student support, interventions, and comprehensive reporting. You will play a critical role in supporting student retention and achievement by providing timely, expert responses to student enquiries and using learning analytics to track progress, identify risks, and engage relevant stakeholders in supporting student success. The Program Delivery Officer also contributes to continuous improvement initiatives, helping to enhance academic administration through innovative and responsive work practices. About you Hold a degree with subsequent relevant experience in student program support/engagement/success (preferably for online students), or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and/or education/training. What we can offer This is a continuing opportunity based at the Logan campus. As Griffith is a multi-site University you may be required to work across other locations. Griffith University’s sites are located on the lands of the Yugarabul, Yuggera, Jagera, Turrbal, Yugambeh and Kombumerri peoples. Salary HEW 6 – Base range - $94,966.18 - $101,295.51 + 17% super. Full package range - $111,110.42 - $118,515.75. Additional Information Why join Griffith? As a values-led organisation, at Griffith University, we've worked hard to create a dynamic and strong organisational culture. We offer: Wide range of Learning and Development opportunities Mix of on campus and work from home options available and a supportive work environment Salary packaging options and corporate health discounts Generous leave entitlements including paid parental leave and leave loading Support with future learning opportunities through our educational staff assistance scheme Opportunities for internal mobility Health Safety and Wellbeing initiatives – on campus Gym facilities At Griffith, we’re committed to providing a safe and inclusive environment for all - whoever you are and wherever you’re from. If you require any accommodations, we welcome you to let us know so we can work with you to participate fully in our recruitment experience. Griffith University values diversity, inclusion and flexibility and we encourage Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, and people of all backgrounds to apply. For more information please visit our Equity, Diversity and Inclusion page. Our University is committed to fostering a safe, respectful and inclusive community for all. In alignment with the National Higher Education Code to Prevent and Respond to Gender-based Violence (2025), Griffith University includes a declaration as part of the recruitment journey to uphold the values and standards of our community. Griffith University also maintains a strict zero-tolerance policy against all forms of modern slavery. For more information, please refer to Griffith’s Modern Slavery Policy . How to apply Please submit your application online and ensure it includes the following: A covering letter outlining your suitability for the role, please refer to the qualifications above and the position description. Current curriculum vitae/resume including full contact details For application and recruitment advice please reach out to Laura Whitworth, Talent Acquisition Partner on l.whitworth-matthews@griffith.edu.au Closing date: Thursday 26th November at 11:59PM - All applications must be submitted online. By clicking the link above or any third-party link within this posting, you are leaving this site and going to a third-party website where the third-party website's terms and privacy policy apply Job Location Google Maps requires functional cookies to be enabled I'm interested I'm interested Privacy Notice Cookies Settings I'm interested Refer a friend share this job Other jobs at Griffith University Lecturer Level B - Human Systems and Exercise Physiology Southport, Australia Technical Officer - Simulation and Practical Experience (SPE) Meadowbrook, Australia Learning Design Support Officer Meadowbrook, Australia Show all jobs Share to WeChat × Copy the link and open WeChat to share. Copy to clipboard Open WeChat Share to WeChat × Use Scan QR Code in WeChat and click ··· to share. Program Delivery Officer 68 University Dr, Meadowbrook QLD 4131, Australia Full-time I'm interested I'm interested"
    }
